{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013jZTU48ic8VoiKEx1WkZvX","type":"tool_result","content":"1380\t- **Uniform:** cream jerseys and pants `#f4ecd8`, navy trim, cap and belt `#1e2a5a`, gold socks `#f2c230`.\n1381\t- **Mascot:** Popcorn Pete, a cream Blob with butter-yellow spots and feet.\n1382\t- **Team super pitch:** **Corn Popper**: the ball pops three times in flight like a kernel, jittering ±3 U at each pop\n1383\t  with a \"pok!\" sound.\n1384\t- **Lineup:**\n1385\t\n1386\t| Pos | Name | B/T | POW CON SPD ARM GLV (pitchers: VEL CTL BRK STA) | Look and notes |\n1387\t|---|---|---|---|---|\n1388\t| CF | **Dot \"Dynamite\" Delgado** (captain) | R/R | 9 8 7 7 7 | heroic build, ponytail, warm brown skin; wields the Batzooka; voice pulse12 300 Hz |\n1389\t| SS | Pep Porter | L/R | 4 8 9 7 9 | twin; chibi build, freckles |\n1390\t| 2B | Pip Porter | R/R | 4 7 9 6 8 | Pep's twin, mirror palette |\n1391\t| 1B | Moose Magnusson | L/L | 9 5 3 5 6 | bulky, blond braid |\n1392\t| 3B | Sunny Sato | R/R | 6 7 6 8 8 | always smiling (`expr: 'smile'`) |\n1393\t| C | Rosa \"Radar\" Reyes | R/R | 6 6 4 9 8 | mask, catcher's mitt |\n1394\t| LF | Lefty Luna | L/L | 5 8 8 6 7 | slap hitter |\n1395\t| RF | Hank \"Hambone\" Hollis | R/R | 8 5 5 9 6 | bulky; eats between pitches |\n1396\t| P | **Grandpa Ike Kowalski** | R/R | 4 8 9 6 | hunch .3, bald, white sides; signature **Butterfly Knuckler**; voice triangle 170 Hz, shaky; the coach |\n1397\t| RP | Kid Kernel | R/R | 9 5 5 4 | teenager; all heat |\n1398\t\n1399\t**2. Harbor City KRAKENS** (HCK). Home: Barnacle Bay Park.\n1400\t- **Uniform:** teal `#1f8a8a`, coral trim `#ff7a5c`, sand pants `#e8d8b0`, sailor-stripe socks.\n1401\t- **Mascot:** Squidge, a purple Blob with a big mouth.\n1402\t- **Captain and ace:** **Captain Bettina Brine** (P, R/L, 7 7 8 7). Signature **Riptide Curve** (a curve that dips,\n1403\t  rises and dips: a sine of amplitude 4 U along its path). Team super **Tidal Wave** (the ball rides a translucent wave\n1404\t  sprite that rises 10 U and crashes down through the zone). Voice: pulse at 200 Hz.\n1405\t- **Lineup:** C \"Barnacle\" Barney Finn · 1B Coral Quinn · 2B Skip Marlin · SS Wade Waters · 3B Gil Gruber ·\n1406\t  LF Shelly Shoals · CF Dash Seaborne · RF Hook Hardy · RP Rip Tidewell.\n1407\t\n1408\t**3. Magma City ERUPTORS** (MCE). Home: Caldera Field.\n1409\t- **Uniform:** charcoal `#2b2b30`, lava orange `#ff6a1a` with yellow trim; caps with flame bills.\n1410\t- **Mascot:** Sparky, a glowing orange Blob that drips embers.\n1411\t- **Captain and ace:** **Iggy \"The Igniter\" Blaze** (P, R/R, 9 6 7 7). Signature **Magma Sinker** (a late drop of\n1412\t  −10 U with an ember trail). Team super **Meteor Heater** (a fireball at 1.35× speed with a flame trail and heat\n1413\t  shimmer; the catcher's mitt smokes). Voice: square at 230 Hz, fast. He is a hothead, and he starts the Tour's\n1414\t  scripted Rhubarb.\n1415\t- **Lineup:** C Basalt Bruno · 1B Magnus Holt · 2B Cinder Ellis · SS Ashley Pyre · 3B \"Hot Corner\" Hector Flores ·\n1416\t  LF Ember Okafor · CF Flint Rocha · RF Sol Vulcan · RP Scorch McGee.\n1417\t\n1418\t**4. Moonbase METEORS** (MBM). Home: Tranquility Dome.\n1419\t- **Uniform:** silver `#c8d0e0`, cosmic purple `#6a4cff`, white; `hat: 'visor'` space helmets in the field.\n1420\t- **Mascot:** Moonpie, a grey cratered Blob that floats.\n1421\t- **Captain and ace:** **Commander Cosmo Vega** (P, L/L, 6 8 9 8). Signature **Zero-G Floater** (slow, 0.62×; it\n1422\t  rises 6 U and then drops 12 U late). Team super **Black Hole Ball** (the ball shrinks to a dot with a dark swirl,\n1423\t  and a batter's reticle within 10 U is pulled 3 U toward it). Voice: sine at 210 Hz with vibrato.\n1424\t- **Lineup:** C Orbit Okoye · 1B Nova Nakamura · 2B Stella Petrov · SS Quasar Diaz · 3B Rocket Rhodes ·\n1425\t  LF Astra Bell · CF Halley Brooks · RF Gus Gravitas · RP Pulsar Penn.\n1426\t\n1427\t**5. Hollowmoor HAUNTS** (HMH). Home: Boneyard Ballpark. Players are `build: 'skeleton'` with `colors.bone`.\n1428\t- **Uniform:** bone `#e8e0c8`, midnight `#1a1630`, ghost green `#7dffb0`; tattered caps.\n1429\t- **Mascot:** Boo, a white Blob with a front face, drawn translucent.\n1430\t- **Captain and ace:** **Count Rattlebones** (P, R/R, 7 8 9 9). Signature **Phantom Forkball** (invisible for\n1431\t  u 0.35–0.8, then a sharp −8 U drop). Team super **Banshee Ball** (invisible until u 0.85, with a scream sound and\n1432\t  a screen flicker). Voice: triangle at 220 Hz with clacks.\n1433\t- **Lineup:** C Mort Graves · 1B Boney Malone · 2B Wailin' Winnie · SS Skelly Kelly · 3B Ezekiel Tomb · LF Shade Murphy ·\n1434\t  CF Wisp O'Hara · RF Digger Doyle · RP Spook Hennessy.\n1435\t\n1436\t**6. MegaMax MECHANICALS** (MMX). The boss team. Home: the MegaMax MegaDome. Players are robot Humanoids: metal\n1437\tcolors, `eyeGlow`, helmets, and `build: 'bulky'` for some.\n1438\t- **Uniform:** chrome `#b8c0cc`, corporate red `#e01e3c`, neon cyan `#2de2e6`.\n1439\t- **Mascot:** Mr. Synergy, a chrome Blob with wings: a hovering drone with a smiley screen.\n1440\t- **Ace and boss:** **ENFORCER-9000** (P, R/R, 10 8 6 10, `size: 2.2`, bulky, red eye glow). Signature **Gigavolt\n1441\t  Heater** (1.25× with an electric zig-zag of ±2 U). Team super **Overclock Laser** (1.5×, perfectly straight, with a\n1442\t  laser trail; only hittable with a GOOD timing or better).\n1443\t- **Boss rules:**\n1444\t  - **Overclock:** his pitch speed rises 5% each inning.\n1445\t  - **Short circuit:** a home run off him short-circuits him for the next half-inning: speed ×0.85, sparks, a\n1446\t    stutter in his windup.\n1447\t  - **Rally Cap:** if the Comets trail entering their last turn at bat, the stands (full of the beaten rival teams)\n1448\t    start the Rally Cap chant and the Comets' meter fills.\n1449\t- **Lineup:** C Backstop-X · 1B Forklift · 2B Servo · SS Sprocket · 3B Torque · LF Router · CF Byte · RF Piston ·\n1450\t  RP Spare Part.\n1451\t\n1452\t**Non-players:**\n1453\t- **Mortimer Megamax:** the villain, owner of MegaMax Corp. `outfit: 'coat'`, `hat: 'tophat'` (§3.3), a gold watch\n1454\t  chain; voice saw at 140 Hz. He watches from a luxury box in the MegaDome.\n1455\t- **HAP HARRIGAN:** headset band, sweater vest.\n1456\t- **BIG LOU BOMBECK:** bulky, bald, a 1979 championship ring.\n1457\t- **GLORIA VOX:** the PA, a portrait only.\n1458\t- **UMPIRE BARB HAMMERSMITH:** navy coat, cap and mask.\n1459\t- **Grounds crew, vendors, fans:** generic rigs and the crowd.\n1460\t\n1461\t### 7.2 Parks (`51-parks.js`)\n1462\t\n1463\t| Park | Team | Time and sky | Fence LF / LC / CF / RC / RF (U), height | Ground beyond | Lights | Weather | Music |\n1464\t|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n1465\t| **Kernel Field** | Comets | golden late afternoon: a custom Backdrop with hills, farmland, a windmill, clouds, a low sun | 980 / 1080 / 1180 / 1060 / 950, h 40 | cornfield (rows of `cornstalk` shapes), the silo in right, a red-barn scoreboard | ambient 0.85, warm sun tint; string lights come on in the evening | light leaves | county-fair organ |\n1466\t| **Barnacle Bay Park** | Krakens | bright noon: the `ocean` preset plus gulls | 1000 / 1100 / 1150 / 1000 / 900 (RF h 30), others h 40 | the bay beyond right (a `water` floor with bobbing boats), a pier, a lighthouse in left | lights off (day) | wind out to left | 6/8 shanty |\n1467\t| **Caldera Field** | Eruptors | dusk: a dark red sky, the volcano, a smoke plume | 920 / 1060 / 1200 / 1100 / 1000, h 50 (basalt) | a lava moat (a `lava` floor, glowing `[r, g, b, glow]`), basalt columns | ambient 0.55; orange lava lights along the fence; 4 light towers | ash | minor drums, saw bass |\n1468\t| **Tranquility Dome** | Meteors | lunar night: the `space` preset, a big Earth disc, the dome's ribs drawn as arcs | 1350 / 1450 / 1550 / 1450 / 1350, h 60 | regolith with craters, habitat modules, antennas, a rover | ambient 0.55; cold blue-white floods | none (\"no air, no wind, no excuses\") | spacey arpeggios |\n1469\t| **Boneyard Ballpark** | Haunts | midnight: a full moon and fog layers | 1000 / 1080 / 1120 / 1080 / 1000, h 36 (an iron cemetery fence) | tombstones, crypts, dead trees, lanterns, candles | ambient 0.45; green and blue lanterns; jack-o'-lantern glow | `leaves` weather, plus fog as Backdrop `fog` layers | spooky organ, theremin |\n1470\t| **MegaMax MegaDome** | Mechanicals | neon night: the `city-night` preset seen through the dome's glass ribs, holo-billboards | 1000 / 1060 / 1100 / 1060 / 1000, h 40; the **Mega Wall** in left (θ −45° to −20°) is h 90 | a neon concourse floor (cyan grid lines), the luxury box, drones | ambient 0.6; magenta and cyan neon lights; the MEGA-TRON's glow | none (indoors) | synthwave |\n1471\t\n1472\t**Per-park physics** (in the park def): `gravityMul` (moon 0.55), `evMul` (moon 0.8), `jumpMul` (moon 2.0), `bounceMul`\n1473\t(dome turf 1.1), and the outfielders' depth shift (moon +200 U). **Floor materials:** grass with the park's mow pattern\n1474\t(Kernel stripes, Barnacle checkerboard, Caldera dark burnt grass, Tranquility bright astroturf, Boneyard dead brown-green,\n1475\tMegaDome turf with cyan neon lines).\n1476\t\n1477\t### 7.3 Pitch catalog (`11-pitch.js` data)\n1478\t\n1479\tThe heater's base speed is 340 U/s. Break is in U at the plate (+x is toward the glove side for a right-handed\n1480\tpitcher); k is the lateness exponent.\n1481\t\n1482\t| Pitch | Speed × | Break x, z | k | Special |\n1483\t|---|---|---|---|---|\n1484\t| Heater (fastball) | 1.00 | 0, +1.5 | 1.0 | a little \"rise\" |\n1485\t| Curve (\"Uncle Charlie\") | 0.74 | +7, −10 | 2.2 | |\n1486\t| Slider | 0.86 | +9, −3 | 2.0 | |\n1487\t| Changeup (\"the Pillow\") | 0.66 | −3, −6 | 1.6 | |\n1488\t| Sinker | 0.92 | −4, −6 | 1.8 | |\n1489\t| Knuckler | 0.60 | 0, −3 | – | wobble: noise of amplitude 4 at 3 Hz from the pitch's own seed |\n1490\t| *Signatures* | | | | Butterfly Knuckler (knuckler ×1.6 wobble, it flutters), Riptide Curve, Magma Sinker, Zero-G Floater, Phantom Forkball, Gigavolt Heater (§7.1) |\n1491\t| *Team supers* | ×1.35 unless stated | | | Corn Popper, Tidal Wave, Meteor Heater, Black Hole Ball, Banshee Ball, Overclock Laser (§7.1) |\n1492\t| Pitch-O-Matic (Derby) | 0.80 | small random breaks from `rng.deal` | – | 80% in the zone; every 5th is a Golden Ball |\n1493\t\n1494\tRepertoires: Ike (heater, curve, knuckler, Butterfly); Kid Kernel (heater, slider, changeup, signature = a 1.15×\n1495\t\"Kernel Cannon\" heater); each rival ace (heater, curve or slider, changeup or sinker, signature); relievers (heater,\n1496\tslider, changeup, the team's signature).\n1497\t\n1498\t### 7.4 Supers\n1499\t\n1500\tThe supers are specified in §6.7; each team's super pitch is in §7.1. **Everyone shares** the Batzooka swing (the\n1501\tComets' bat is \"the original\"; rivals have knock-offs drawn in their team colors: the \"Krakenzooka\", \"Lavazooka\",\n1502\t\"Lunazooka\", \"Ghoulzooka\" and \"MEGAZOOKA 9000\"), Laser Arm and Afterburners.\n1503\t\n1504\t### 7.5 The Tour: story and cutscenes (`52-story.js`)\n1505\t\n1506\t**The story.** Kernel Field, home of the Comets since forever, is about to become a parking lot. Mortimer Megamax bets\n1507\tthe deed on the Kaboom Cup, a barnstorming tour of the wildest parks in baseball. The Comets' secret weapon is\n1508\tGrandma Delgado's homemade Batzooka, which only fires when the crowd roars. Each stop is a cutscene (in the Broadcast\n1509\tCam, with rigs, poses and dialog portraits), then the game (with scripted radio lines when its hazard first shows),\n1510\tthen a post-game scene.\n1511\t\n1512\t**Prologue: \"Last Game at Kernel Field?\"** (Kernel Field at dusk, after a practice)\n1513\t- HAP: \"Good evening, baseball fans, from Kernel Field, where the corn is high and the stakes are higher!\"\n1514\t- *A limousine rolls up the foul line. A bulldozer follows it.*\n1515\t- MORTIMER: \"Enjoy your little cornfield, Comets. Monday it's a parking lot. Premium spaces only.\"\n1516\t- DOT: \"Over my dead batting glove.\"\n1517\t- MORTIMER: \"Win the Kaboom Cup and I'll tear up the deed. Lose, and I pave the park AND hang that bat in my lobby.\"\n1518\t- IKE: *(opens a dusty crate)* \"Your grandma's BATZOOKA. Hickory, duct tape and a surplus bottle rocket. Summer of '62.\"\n1519\t- DOT: \"What does it do?\"\n1520\t- IKE: \"Nothin'. Till the crowd gets loud. Then it does EVERYTHING.\"\n1521\t- LOU: \"Folks, I haven't seen a bat that dangerous since I swung at my own shadow in '79!\"\n1522\t- → Offer Spring Training (\"Learn the ropes with Grandpa Ike?\" PLAY · SKIP), then the Tour Map.\n1523\t\n1524\t**Stop 1: Barnacle Bay Park vs the Krakens.**\n1525\t- *Pregame:* BRINE: \"Ahoy, corn-pickers! The tide's coming in, and it's bringing a whole ocean of hurt!\" DOT: \"We\n1526\t  brought sunscreen.\" LOU: \"Watch the gulls, folks. They've got better hands than my old infield.\"\n1527\t- *First gull snatch:* HAP: \"A seagull just stole a fly ball! Is that legal? Barb says it's... in play!\"\n1528\t- *Win:* BRINE: \"Blast it all. Take this. Barnacle Grip Tape. Sticks to anything, except a lead.\" (Lumber +1.)\n1529\t- *Loss:* BRINE: \"Back to the shallow end, landlubbers!\"\n1530\t\n1531\t**Stop 2: Caldera Field vs the Eruptors.**\n1532\t- *Pregame:* IGGY: \"Hope you packed sunscreen. SPF one million.\" IKE: \"Don't stand on anything that's glowing.\"\n1533\t- *First vent:* HAP: \"The ground just sneezed lava, and the baseball went with it!\"\n1534\t- *Scripted Rhubarb* (the first time Iggy hits a batter, or in the 2nd inning by script): LOU: \"Uh-oh, the benches\n1535\t  are emptying! Somebody fetch a fire extinguisher and a referee!\" BARB (after): \"Everybody back in your dugouts\n1536\t  before I eject the volcano!\"\n1537\t- *Win:* IGGY: \"You've got fire, Delgado. Here. Magma Cleats. They're only a little bit on fire.\" (Jet Cleats +1.)\n1538\t\n1539\t**Stop 3: Tranquility Dome vs the Meteors.**\n1540\t- *Pregame:* COSMO: \"Welcome to the Moon, Comets. Up here every pop fly is a field trip.\" HANK: \"Is there a snack bar\n1541\t  on the Moon?\" LOU: \"Gravity took the day off, folks. Somebody tell the baseball.\"\n1542\t- *First meteor shower:* HAP: \"Meteor shower in left field! The grounds crew is going to need a bigger rake!\"\n1543\t- *Win:* COSMO: \"Mission accomplished, for you. Zero-G Gloves. They catch whatever gravity drops.\" (Glue Gloves +1.)\n1544\t\n1545\t**Stop 4: Boneyard Ballpark vs the Haunts.**\n1546\t- *Pregame:* RATTLEBONES: \"We've been dying to play you. Literally. Since 1887.\" PIP: \"I'm not scared.\" PEP: \"You're\n1547\t  holding my hand.\" PIP: \"You're holding MINE.\"\n1548\t- *First Phantom Fog:* HAP: \"Where'd it go?! The ball just turned into a rumor!\"\n1549\t- *Win:* RATTLEBONES: \"A fine game, mortals. Phantom Pine Tar. It makes the crowd scream louder.\" (Hype Machine +1.)\n1550\t\n1551\t**Stop 5 (the final): the MegaMax MegaDome vs the Mechanicals, for the Kaboom Cup.**\n1552\t- *Pregame:* MORTIMER (on the MEGA-TRON): \"Meet my ace. Ninety thousand horsepower. Zero feelings. ENFORCER-9000!\"\n1553\t  ENFORCER: \"PREPARE. TO. BE. STRUCK. OUT.\" DOT: \"Then let's give him some feelings.\" IKE: \"Swing when they roar,\n1554\t  kid.\"\n1555\t- *First short circuit:* LOU: \"He's smoking! I mean really smoking! Somebody unplug that fella!\"\n1556\t- *Rally Cap* (if trailing in the last inning): HAP: \"Listen to this! The Krakens, the Eruptors, the Meteors, even\n1557\t  the Haunts! They're ALL chanting for the Comets!\" (meter → 100)\n1558\t- *Win, the ending:*\n1559\t  1. The Batzooka's last moonshot hits the MEGA-TRON, which rains sparks.\n1560\t  2. MORTIMER: \"My jumbotron! My deed! My... reputation!\"\n1561\t  3. The deed flutters into the Batzooka's backblast and burns to confetti.\n1562\t  4. DOT: \"Kernel Field stays. Same time next season?\"\n1563\t  5. ENFORCER: \"...I. LIKE. BASEBALL.\"\n1564\t  6. **Credits** roll over a blooper reel: rigs doing pratfalls, Hank eating, the mascot race tumble. Then \"THE END?\n1565\t     Exhibition: everything unlocked.\"\n1566\t- *Loss:* MORTIMER: \"Pave it! Pave it all!\" → RAIN CHECK.\n1567\t\n1568\t### 7.6 Spring Training lessons (`53-lessons.js`)\n1569\t\n1570\tEach lesson: Ike's intro (two lines), a drill with an on-screen goal (\"3 / 3 FAIR BALLS\"), prompts, and \"LESSON\n1571\tPASSED!\". Lessons 1–2 have slow motion ×0.6 on the first pitches.\n1572\t\n1573\t| # | Lesson | Drill | Passed when |\n1574\t|---|---|---|---|\n1575\t| 1 | **Batting Practice** | slow heaters from Ike; aim and time the contact swing | 3 fair balls |\n1576\t| 2 | **Power and Bunts** | power swings at meatballs, then bunt | 1 home run with a power swing and 1 fair bunt |\n1577\t| 3 | **Reading the Zone** | a mix of strikes and balls, curves included | take 2 balls and hit 2 strikes |\n1578\t| 4 | **On the Mound** | you pitch to a CPU batter | 3 strikes with 3 different pitches, one PERFECT release, one aftertouch |\n1579\t| 5 | **Leather and Lasers** | fielding: Ike hits flies and grounders | 2 fly catches, a grounder thrown to first in time, a double play |\n1580\t| 6 | **Wheels** | baserunning | advance on a hit, tag up on a fly, steal second, use turbo, slide in safe |\n1581\t| 7 | **BATZOOKA!** | the meter is pre-filled | hit a Batzooka home run, throw a super pitch, make a Laser Arm throw |\n1582\t| 8 | **Rhubarb 101** | a practice brawl with the grounds crew | land 5 punches, 1 shove and 1 toss |\n1583\t| – | **House Rules** card | what you can't do (§6.1) | – |\n1584\t\n1585\t### 7.7 Derby\n1586\t\n1587\tRules are in §6.18. Targets by park: the blimp (every park but the moon dome, which has a satellite instead), the\n1588\tjumbotron or scoreboard, the bullseye on the batter's eye, and drones at the MegaDome. The hub round uses the\n1589\tMegaDome.\n1590\t\n1591\t### 7.8 Clubhouse upgrades (`55-upgrades.js`)\n1592\t\n1593\t| Upgrade | Per tier | Costs (FB) for tiers 1 / 2 / 3 |\n1594\t|---|---|---|\n1595\t| Lumber | exit speed +5% | 400 / 800 / 1400 |\n1596\t| Glue Gloves | catch radius +1 U, catch chance +2% | 300 / 700 / 1200 |\n1597\t| Jet Cleats | run and field speed +4% | 300 / 700 / 1200 |\n1598\t| Cannon Arms | throws +5%, pitch speed +3% | 400 / 800 / 1400 |\n1599\t| Hype Machine | meter gain +10% | 500 / 1000 / 1600 |\n1600\t\n1601\tThe clubhouse screen is five big cards with a picture, the tier pips, the cost and \"✕ BUY\". Grandpa Ike comments on\n1602\teach purchase.\n1603\t\n1604\t### 7.9 Commentary line pools (`54-lines.js`)\n1605\t\n1606\tAt least 6 lines per tag (and 10 for the most common: strike, ball, foul, single, out). Samples in the voice to\n1607\tmatch:\n1608\t\n1609\t| Tag | Samples |\n1610\t|---|---|\n1611\t| `batter_up` (PA) | \"Now batting... number seven... DOT... DYNAMITE... DELGADO!\" |\n1612\t| `strike_called` | \"Strike one, right on the black. You could hang a picture on that one.\" |\n1613\t| `strike_swinging` | \"Swing and a miss! He swung so hard he unscrewed himself from the box!\" |\n1614\t| `ball` | \"Ball, low. That one was dragging its feet.\" |\n1615\t| `foul_back` | \"Fouled straight back! Duck, Lou!\" / LOU: \"I've been ducking since '79.\" |\n1616\t| `strikeout` | \"Strike three! Back to the dugout to think about what he's done.\" |\n1617\t| `walk` | \"Ball four. Take your base, and take a sandwich while you're at it.\" |\n1618\t| `single` | \"Seeing-eye single through the right side! That ball had a map and a flashlight.\" |\n1619\t| `double` | \"Into the gap! {batter} is digging for second like there's buried treasure!\" |\n1620\t| `triple` | \"Off the wall, he's rounding second, he's going for three! He's SAFE!\" |\n1621\t| `homer` | \"Swung on and BELTED! Deep! Way back! That ball has left the zip code!\" / \"{dist} feet! They'll need a passport to bring that one back!\" |\n1622\t| `batzooka_ready` | \"The crowd is ROARING! You know what that means... it's BATZOOKA TIME!\" |\n1623\t| `batzooka_hit` | \"KA-BLAMMO! That's not a home run, that's a space program!\" |\n1624\t| `batzooka_fizzle` | \"Fizzle! That's the loudest nothing I've ever heard.\" |\n1625\t| `super_pitch` | \"{pitcher} just threw a pitch that's probably illegal in three states!\" |\n1626\t| `catch_dive` | \"Laid out like a welcome mat! What a grab!\" |\n1627\t| `robbery` | \"He climbed the wall and STOLE it! Call the sheriff!\" |\n1628\t| `error` | \"Clank! You could hear that one in the next county.\" |\n1629\t| `double_play` | \"Two for the price of one! Around the horn and back for a nap!\" |\n1630\t| `steal_safe` | \"He's stealing! ...SAFE! Lock up your valuables, folks.\" |\n1631\t| `bowl_over` | \"COLLISION AT THE PLATE! Somebody check the catcher's warranty!\" |\n1632\t| `rhubarb_start` | \"Here come the benches! It's a rhubarb, folks, a genuine dust-up!\" |\n1633\t| `rhubarb_end` | \"Barb's breaking it up. Everybody's dusting off. Nobody's going home, though everybody's going home dirty.\" |\n1634\t| `walkoff` | \"WALK-OFF! The {team} win it! Pile on, pile on!\" (only a home team can walk off; in the Tour the Comets are always the visitors) |\n1635\t| `lead_change` | \"And just like that, we've got ourselves a brand-new ballgame!\" |\n1636\t| `hazard_*` | one pool per park (§7.5's first-time lines plus 5 more each) |\n1637\t| `between` | \"Time for the Mascot Race! My money's on the popcorn.\" |\n1638\t| `umpire` (stamps + voice) | \"STEE-RIIIKE!\" \"BALL!\" \"YER OUT!\" \"SAFE!\" \"FAIR BALL!\" \"FOUL!\" \"PLAY BALL!\" \"TIME!\" |\n1639\t| `vendor` | \"PEANUTS!\" \"GET YER DOGS!\" \"COLD LEMONADE!\" |\n1640\t\n1641\t### 7.10 Music\n1642\t\n1643\tThe list is in §6.16. Every song is written in the engine's notation in `56-songs.js` (a melody, bass and drums at\n1644\tleast; organ voicing for the ballpark tunes; named layers for in-game loops).\n1645\t\n1646\t### 7.11 Attract reel segments (`35-attract.js`)\n1647\t\n1648\t| # | Segment (caption) | Park | What's forced | ≈ s |\n1649\t|---|---|---|---|---|\n1650\t| 1 | \"PLAY BALL!\" | Kernel Field | the title flyover, then a pitch duel in the Plate Cam: a called strike, a foul back, then a line-drive single and the throw in | 18 |\n1651\t| 2 | \"SUPER PITCHES\" | Caldera | Iggy's Meteor Heater for a swinging strike three; then a fly ball launched by a lava vent | 15 |\n1652\t| 3 | \"LEATHER AND LASERS\" | Barnacle Bay | a diving catch in right; a gull snatches a fly; a Laser Arm throw home, a slide and a bowl-over | 20 |\n1653\t| 4 | \"WHEELS\" | Kernel Field | a steal of second with a headfirst dive; turbo | 12 |\n1654\t| 5 | \"BATZOOKA!\" | MegaDome | Dot arms the Batzooka: the moonshot, the Moonshot Cam, the MEGA-TRON explodes, fireworks, the trot | 20 |\n1655\t| 6 | \"RHUBARB!\" | Caldera | HBP into the brawl: fight clouds; Barb breaks it up | 14 |\n1656\t| 7 | \"SIX WILD PARKS\" | Tranquility | a low-gravity fly; the CF climbs the wall 3× high for a robbery | 14 |\n1657\t| 8 | (continued) | Boneyard | the Banshee Ball (an invisible pitch) for a whiff; a ghost wall catch | 14 |\n1658\t| 9 | \"1–4 PLAYERS · PLAY ONLINE IN AI HUB\" | MegaDome | Derby swings with three ghost comets (local fakes) | 15 |\n1659\t| 10 | \"MOONSHOT LEADERS\" | – | the high-score table, then the title logo and \"PRESS START\" | 10 |\n1660\t\n1661\t### 7.12 Art assets to make (`04-shapes.js`, code-drawn sprites)\n1662\t\n1663\tUse the engine's core library where it fits (`barrel`, `crate`, `bench`, `fence`, `tree`, `pine`, `rock`, `bush`,\n1664\t`lamppost`, `sign`, `cart`, `table`) and props (`lamp`, `streetlamp`, `banner`, `torch`, `brazier`, `firedrum`, `candle`,\n1665\t`lantern`, `pot`, `skull`, `cobweb`). Write new `E.SHAPES` entries (check each with `node tools/asset-sheet.mjs`) for:\n1666\t- **Every park:** the base (a white pillow), home plate, the rubber, the mound, the foul pole, the dugout bench, the\n1667\t  bat rack, the helmet rack, the water cooler, the rosin bag, a light tower (with `lights:`), a scoreboard frame, the\n1668\t  jumbotron frame, the batting-practice L-screen, the batting cage net, the Pitch-O-Matic 3000.\n1669\t- **Kernel Field:** cornstalk, silo, hay bale, red-barn scoreboard, windmill, windsock.\n1670\t- **Barnacle Bay:** lighthouse, boat, buoy, pier piling, lobster trap.\n1671\t- **Caldera:** basalt column, lava vent (cone, with glow), warning sign.\n1672\t- **Tranquility:** habitat module, antenna, satellite dish, rover, airlock.\n1673\t- **Boneyard:** tombstone (3 shapes by seed), crypt, iron fence section, jack-o'-lantern.\n1674\t- **MegaDome:** holo-billboard, drone, luxury box, MEGA-TRON.\n1675\t\n1676\t**Code-drawn sprites:** the ball (5×5, with stitches, 2 rotating frames), the blimp, gulls (a Blob with wings), the\n1677\tlanding marker, the reticles (contact: a thin ring; power: a thick red ring; Batzooka: a ring of fire), the pitch\n1678\ttarget and release ring, the zone grid, base rings, the glyph icons (§6.13), the meter gauges, the scorebug, the\n1679\tBatzooka overdraw (nozzle, fins and a glowing barrel over the bat in the hands), the fight cloud, popcorn, confetti\n1680\tand fireworks.\n1681\t\n1682\t---\n1683\t\n1684\t## 8. Art and animation\n1685\t\n1686\t### 8.1 Look (the engine's own look target, applied)\n1687\t\n1688\tTASK.md puts frame-rate targets and optimization out of scope, so add as much detail as each scene needs: big\n1689\tcrowds, many lights, particles, shadows and props.\n1690\t\n1691\t1. **Resolution:** `res: 'ps1'`, `expand: true`. The HUD anchors to `r.W` and `r.H`. Rigs are `size: 1.15–1.35`\n1692\t   (bosses 2.2); props use `propSize: 1.3`.\n1693\t2. **Dressed characters:** every player gets the team uniform, plus hair, skin, build and size of their own, and the\n1694\t   gear for their job (below). Nobody keeps the defaults.\n1695\t3. **Backdrops:** every park's sky is an `E.Backdrop` (§7.2), seen in the Plate Cam and the Moonshot Cam. The Broadcast\n1696\t   Cam shows ground to the screen's edges (the park continues past the stands; `map.outside` is the park's ground\n1697\t   color).\n1698\t4. **Textures:** grass with grain and a mow pattern, dirt with speckle, chalk lines slightly worn, the warning track,\n1699\t   padded fence faces, stone or plank stands.\n1700\t5. **Props on every screen:** dugouts, bat racks, coolers, light towers, poles, the park's own pieces (§7.12), 3–8 in\n1701\t   any Broadcast Cam view.\n1702\t6. **Effects on every hit** (§8.4).\n1703\t7. **Color:** everything drawn by hand is shaded with `E.tones` and `E.ramp`.\n1704\t8. **Type:** the `E.font.title` logo and stamps; HUD text with shadows; `E.ui.box` gradient panels.\n1705\t9. **Light:** night parks run `game.lights` with tower floods and local glows; day parks a warm high ambient.\n1706\t   Emissive for fire, neon, lasers and the Batzooka.\n1707\t10. **Faces in dialog:** every speaker has a live portrait (`rig.drawPortrait`), the announcers included.\n1708\t\n1709\t### 8.2 Rigs and uniforms (`03-rigs.js`)\n1710\t\n1711\t`BZ.makeRig(player, team, job)` builds an `E.Humanoid` from the team's colors and the player's looks:\n1712\t\n1713\t| Job | Kit |\n1714\t|---|---|\n1715\t| batter | `hat: 'batting'` in the team color, `weapon: 'bat'`, `grip: 'both'`, batting gloves (`colors.glove`) |\n1716\t| fielder | `hat: 'cap'`, `mitt: 'fielder'` (`'first'` for 1B) |\n1717\t| catcher | `hat: 'mask'`, `armor: true` (the chest protector, `plate` = the team's dark color), `mitt: 'catcher'` |\n1718\t| pitcher | `hat: 'cap'`, `mitt: 'fielder'` |\n1719\t| runner | `hat: 'batting'`, no bat |\n1720\t| umpire | `outfit: 'coat'` (navy), `hat: 'mask'` |\n1721\t| robots | metal colors, `eyeGlow`, a stiffer gait (`stride` and `swing` lower), sparks when short-circuited |\n1722\t| skeletons | `build: 'skeleton'`, `colors.bone` |\n1723\t| mascots, gulls, ghosts, drones | `E.Blob` (`feet`, `wings`, `mouth`, `face: 'front'`) |\n1724\t\n1725\tRigs are cached per player and job and swapped as the job changes (batter → runner → fielder between halves).\n1726\t\n1727\t### 8.3 New animations\n1728\t\n1729\t**Motion clips.** One set file, `assets/mocap-batzooka.js`:\n1730\t```\n1731\tnode tools/anim-set.mjs <repo>/src/mocap/sets/quaternius.js <repo>/examples/cmu-lib/CMU_124.js <repo>/src/mocap/sets/mesh2motion.js \\\n1732\t  --clips 124_01,124_07,124_08,124_12,QUATERNIUS:Slide_Start,QUATERNIUS:Slide_Loop,QUATERNIUS:Slide_Exit,QUATERNIUS:Punch_Jab,QUATERNIUS:Punch_Cross,Victory,Cheering_Two_Hands \\\n1733\t  --name BATZOOKA --out assets/mocap-batzooka.js\n1734\t```\n1735\tIf a clip name is reported as in two sets, prefix it with `SET:`, as the tool asks. Load `engine/mocap-readable.js`,\n1736\t`engine/mocap.js` and the set after the engine. Then:\n1737\t- `const lib = Mocap.load(MOCAP.BATZOOKA)`, and `Mocap.drive(rig, lib)` once per rig that uses clips.\n1738\t- The CMU takes are long, with several repetitions. Write `tools/clip-windows.mjs` to find one clean window per motion\n1739\t  (the hands' speed peak marks contact or release; the window runs from the last still moment before it to the next\n1740\t  one after it) and store them as data: `{ swing: ['124_07', a, b, contactAt], pitch: ['124_01', a, b, releaseAt], ... }`.\n1741\t- Time-map each window so that its contact or release key lands exactly on the game's moment (the swing delay, the\n1742\t  release time).\n1743\t- `rig.mocapW` fades in and out over 0.08 s. Lefties use `MocapReadable.mirror(clip)`, made once at load.\n1744\t- The bat follows the hands (`rig.mocapBlade = true`, with the `bat` weapon drawn along the knuckle line).\n1745\t- Review every motion with `tools/filmstrip.mjs` on the `#gallery` page. If a clip reads badly at game size, use the\n1746\t  procedural fallback in the table (both are written, and the better one is picked by looking at the strips).\n1747\t\n1748\t| Motion | Source | Notes |\n1749\t|---|---|---|\n1750\t| batting stance and waggle | procedural: the bat up and back, knees bent (`crouch` .3), the bat bobbing on a sine with a per-player tempo | |\n1751\t| contact swing | clip 124_07 window, time-mapped to 0.10 s to the plane | fallback spec `SWING`: `{ rel: true, hand: 'both', a0: 2.4, a1: −2.6, z0: −2, z1: −4, reach: 6, wind: .10, active: .08, recover: .30, lunge: 2.2, twist: 2.2, lean: .25, hold: .35 }` |\n1752\t| power swing | the same window, stretched to 0.14 s, with a bigger stride (root forward 3 U) | fallback: `SWING` with lunge 3, twist 2.8 |\n1753\t| Batzooka swing | the power swing plus a recoil hop (`rig.kick`), muzzle flash and smoke | |\n1754\t| bunt | clip 124_08 window | fallback: the bat held level at the chest with both hands (an IK override) |\n1755\t| windup and pitch | clip 124_01 window (set, leg lift, stride, release, follow-through); mirrored for lefties; the ball leaves `rig.hand()` at the release key | fallback: the `knee` kick spec (leg lift) chained into `throw` (lunge 2.4, lean .6) |\n1756\t| underhand toss (Ike's batting practice, Derby intro) | clip 124_12 | |\n1757\t| fielder's throw | `E.MOVES.throw` plus a crow-hop for outfielders (`hop: .8`) | |\n1758\t| catch high, low and backhand | procedural: after `solvePose`, IK the glove hand to the ball (`E.ik3`); the body turns to it | |\n1759\t| dive | procedural: lean forward and blend `down` 0→1 over 0.2 s while the body slides; the glove reaches out | |\n1760\t| jump catch | `Body.jump` plus `air: true` and the glove IK'd up | |\n1761\t| wall climb | `climb: true` with vz (hand-over-hand) facing the fence; a reach at the top | |\n1762\t| feet-first slide | clips Slide_Start → Slide_Loop → Slide_Exit | |\n1763\t| headfirst dive | procedural: `down` blend, forward lean, both arms out | |\n1764\t| run and turbo | the engine's gait from velocity; turbo uses `sprint: true` (lean) plus speed lines | |\n1765\t| tag | a low swipe with the glove hand (custom spec, `hand: 'L'`) | |\n1766\t| umpire calls | strike: a right-fist punch-out (`cross` with a long `hold`) and `expr: 'shout'`; out: a fist pump (`uppercut`); safe: both arms sweeping out wide (a two-hand spec: a0 1.4 → a1 −0.2) | |\n1767\t| celebrations | clips Victory and Cheering_Two_Hands; `pose: 'cheer'`; high-fives (two rigs meeting); the dugout bounce | |\n1768\t| dejection | `pose: 'kneel'`, `expr: 'wince'` | |\n1769\t| Rhubarb | `E.Combo(['jab', 'cross', 'hook'])` (or clips Punch_Jab and Punch_Cross), `bash`, `throw`, `down` with dizzy stars | |\n1770\t| catcher | the `crouch` pose; the mitt IK'd to the pitch; popping up to throw | |\n1771\t| walk-up | walking with the bat on the shoulder; two practice swings | |\n1772\t| the trot | a jog; high-fives with the base coaches; a cap tip | |\n1773\t\n1774\t### 8.4 Effects\n1775\t\n1776\t- **Contact:** sparks and a ring by Q, a white flash 0.06 s, hit-stop 0.06 s, rumble.\n1777\t- **Broken bat:** on jammed contact (Q < 0.15 against a heater at 1.0× or more, 8% chance from `rng.fx`; cosmetic\n1778\t  only), wood splinters (`particles.bits` in wood colors) and \"CRACK! Broken bat!\" on the radio.\n1779\t- **Pitch trails:** speed lines for heaters; fire for the Meteor Heater; a wave sprite for the Tidal Wave; a dark\n1780\t  swirl for the Black Hole; a shimmer while invisible; a laser line for the Overclock Laser (emissive); popcorn puffs\n1781\t  for the Corn Popper.\n1782\t- **Ball:** a trail above 500 U/s; dust on bounces; sparks off the fence; a splash in water; a lava sizzle; a meteor\n1783\t  crater decal.\n1784\t- **Players:** dust on slides and dives; speed lines on turbo; fire trails for Afterburners; stars and a ring on\n1785\t  collisions; dizzy stars.\n1786\t- **Spectacle:** fireworks (`particles.explosion` small, plus colored sparks), confetti, popcorn, the crowd wave,\n1787\t  scoreboard bulbs, the jumbotron, heat shimmer at Caldera.\n1788\t- **Comfort:** every `shake` and `flash` follows the comfort settings.\n1789\t\n1790\t---\n1791\t\n1792\t## 9. Build order and milestones\n1793\t\n1794\tBuild in this order. Each milestone ends with its tests passing (`node tests/run.mjs`), the bundle building, and a\n1795\tplayable build. Temporary scaffolding inside a milestone is fine, but nothing temporary survives M8.\n1796\t\n1797\t**M0: Foundation.**\n1798\t- Make the dev folder (§4.1) and fetch the sources (§3.1).\n1799\t- `npm install`, then `npx playwright install chromium`. If `/tmp` is full on this shared machine (it was while"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a605ca8e-6f21-4c44-bd74-b97a2b38e121","uuid":"1f92aa6c-fa75-470d-b5b3-6db17cc04c75","timestamp":"2026-11-04T13:01:35.080Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium.build__20261104-060114__x4549c1/work/PLAN.md","content":"- **Uniform:** cream jerseys and pants `#f4ecd8`, navy trim, cap and belt `#1e2a5a`, gold socks `#f2c230`.\n- **Mascot:** Popcorn Pete, a cream Blob with butter-yellow spots and feet.\n- **Team super pitch:** **Corn Popper**: the ball pops three times in flight like a kernel, jittering ±3 U at each pop\n  with a \"pok!\" sound.\n- **Lineup:**\n\n| Pos | Name | B/T | POW CON SPD ARM GLV (pitchers: VEL CTL BRK STA) | Look and notes |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| CF | **Dot \"Dynamite\" Delgado** (captain) | R/R | 9 8 7 7 7 | heroic build, ponytail, warm brown skin; wields the Batzooka; voice pulse12 300 Hz |\n| SS | Pep Porter | L/R | 4 8 9 7 9 | twin; chibi build, freckles |\n| 2B | Pip Porter | R/R | 4 7 9 6 8 | Pep's twin, mirror palette |\n| 1B | Moose Magnusson | L/L | 9 5 3 5 6 | bulky, blond braid |\n| 3B | Sunny Sato | R/R | 6 7 6 8 8 | always smiling (`expr: 'smile'`) |\n| C | Rosa \"Radar\" Reyes | R/R | 6 6 4 9 8 | mask, catcher's mitt |\n| LF | Lefty Luna | L/L | 5 8 8 6 7 | slap hitter |\n| RF | Hank \"Hambone\" Hollis | R/R | 8 5 5 9 6 | bulky; eats between pitches |\n| P | **Grandpa Ike Kowalski** | R/R | 4 8 9 6 | hunch .3, bald, white sides; signature **Butterfly Knuckler**; voice triangle 170 Hz, shaky; the coach |\n| RP | Kid Kernel | R/R | 9 5 5 4 | teenager; all heat |\n\n**2. Harbor City KRAKENS** (HCK). Home: Barnacle Bay Park.\n- **Uniform:** teal `#1f8a8a`, coral trim `#ff7a5c`, sand pants `#e8d8b0`, sailor-stripe socks.\n- **Mascot:** Squidge, a purple Blob with a big mouth.\n- **Captain and ace:** **Captain Bettina Brine** (P, R/L, 7 7 8 7). Signature **Riptide Curve** (a curve that dips,\n  rises and dips: a sine of amplitude 4 U along its path). Team super **Tidal Wave** (the ball rides a translucent wave\n  sprite that rises 10 U and crashes down through the zone). Voice: pulse at 200 Hz.\n- **Lineup:** C \"Barnacle\" Barney Finn · 1B Coral Quinn · 2B Skip Marlin · SS Wade Waters · 3B Gil Gruber ·\n  LF Shelly Shoals · CF Dash Seaborne · RF Hook Hardy · RP Rip Tidewell.\n\n**3. Magma City ERUPTORS** (MCE). Home: Caldera Field.\n- **Uniform:** charcoal `#2b2b30`, lava orange `#ff6a1a` with yellow trim; caps with flame bills.\n- **Mascot:** Sparky, a glowing orange Blob that drips embers.\n- **Captain and ace:** **Iggy \"The Igniter\" Blaze** (P, R/R, 9 6 7 7). Signature **Magma Sinker** (a late drop of\n  −10 U with an ember trail). Team super **Meteor Heater** (a fireball at 1.35× speed with a flame trail and heat\n  shimmer; the catcher's mitt smokes). Voice: square at 230 Hz, fast. He is a hothead, and he starts the Tour's\n  scripted Rhubarb.\n- **Lineup:** C Basalt Bruno · 1B Magnus Holt · 2B Cinder Ellis · SS Ashley Pyre · 3B \"Hot Corner\" Hector Flores ·\n  LF Ember Okafor · CF Flint Rocha · RF Sol Vulcan · RP Scorch McGee.\n\n**4. Moonbase METEORS** (MBM). Home: Tranquility Dome.\n- **Uniform:** silver `#c8d0e0`, cosmic purple `#6a4cff`, white; `hat: 'visor'` space helmets in the field.\n- **Mascot:** Moonpie, a grey cratered Blob that floats.\n- **Captain and ace:** **Commander Cosmo Vega** (P, L/L, 6 8 9 8). Signature **Zero-G Floater** (slow, 0.62×; it\n  rises 6 U and then drops 12 U late). Team super **Black Hole Ball** (the ball shrinks to a dot with a dark swirl,\n  and a batter's reticle within 10 U is pulled 3 U toward it). Voice: sine at 210 Hz with vibrato.\n- **Lineup:** C Orbit Okoye · 1B Nova Nakamura · 2B Stella Petrov · SS Quasar Diaz · 3B Rocket Rhodes ·\n  LF Astra Bell · CF Halley Brooks · RF Gus Gravitas · RP Pulsar Penn.\n\n**5. Hollowmoor HAUNTS** (HMH). Home: Boneyard Ballpark. Players are `build: 'skeleton'` with `colors.bone`.\n- **Uniform:** bone `#e8e0c8`, midnight `#1a1630`, ghost green `#7dffb0`; tattered caps.\n- **Mascot:** Boo, a white Blob with a front face, drawn translucent.\n- **Captain and ace:** **Count Rattlebones** (P, R/R, 7 8 9 9). Signature **Phantom Forkball** (invisible for\n  u 0.35–0.8, then a sharp −8 U drop). Team super **Banshee Ball** (invisible until u 0.85, with a scream sound and\n  a screen flicker). Voice: triangle at 220 Hz with clacks.\n- **Lineup:** C Mort Graves · 1B Boney Malone · 2B Wailin' Winnie · SS Skelly Kelly · 3B Ezekiel Tomb · LF Shade Murphy ·\n  CF Wisp O'Hara · RF Digger Doyle · RP Spook Hennessy.\n\n**6. MegaMax MECHANICALS** (MMX). The boss team. Home: the MegaMax MegaDome. Players are robot Humanoids: metal\ncolors, `eyeGlow`, helmets, and `build: 'bulky'` for some.\n- **Uniform:** chrome `#b8c0cc`, corporate red `#e01e3c`, neon cyan `#2de2e6`.\n- **Mascot:** Mr. Synergy, a chrome Blob with wings: a hovering drone with a smiley screen.\n- **Ace and boss:** **ENFORCER-9000** (P, R/R, 10 8 6 10, `size: 2.2`, bulky, red eye glow). Signature **Gigavolt\n  Heater** (1.25× with an electric zig-zag of ±2 U). Team super **Overclock Laser** (1.5×, perfectly straight, with a\n  laser trail; only hittable with a GOOD timing or better).\n- **Boss rules:**\n  - **Overclock:** his pitch speed rises 5% each inning.\n  - **Short circuit:** a home run off him short-circuits him for the next half-inning: speed ×0.85, sparks, a\n    stutter in his windup.\n  - **Rally Cap:** if the Comets trail entering their last turn at bat, the stands (full of the beaten rival teams)\n    start the Rally Cap chant and the Comets' meter fills.\n- **Lineup:** C Backstop-X · 1B Forklift · 2B Servo · SS Sprocket · 3B Torque · LF Router · CF Byte · RF Piston ·\n  RP Spare Part.\n\n**Non-players:**\n- **Mortimer Megamax:** the villain, owner of MegaMax Corp. `outfit: 'coat'`, `hat: 'tophat'` (§3.3), a gold watch\n  chain; voice saw at 140 Hz. He watches from a luxury box in the MegaDome.\n- **HAP HARRIGAN:** headset band, sweater vest.\n- **BIG LOU BOMBECK:** bulky, bald, a 1979 championship ring.\n- **GLORIA VOX:** the PA, a portrait only.\n- **UMPIRE BARB HAMMERSMITH:** navy coat, cap and mask.\n- **Grounds crew, vendors, fans:** generic rigs and the crowd.\n\n### 7.2 Parks (`51-parks.js`)\n\n| Park | Team | Time and sky | Fence LF / LC / CF / RC / RF (U), height | Ground beyond | Lights | Weather | Music |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| **Kernel Field** | Comets | golden late afternoon: a custom Backdrop with hills, farmland, a windmill, clouds, a low sun | 980 / 1080 / 1180 / 1060 / 950, h 40 | cornfield (rows of `cornstalk` shapes), the silo in right, a red-barn scoreboard | ambient 0.85, warm sun tint; string lights come on in the evening | light leaves | county-fair organ |\n| **Barnacle Bay Park** | Krakens | bright noon: the `ocean` preset plus gulls | 1000 / 1100 / 1150 / 1000 / 900 (RF h 30), others h 40 | the bay beyond right (a `water` floor with bobbing boats), a pier, a lighthouse in left | lights off (day) | wind out to left | 6/8 shanty |\n| **Caldera Field** | Eruptors | dusk: a dark red sky, the volcano, a smoke plume | 920 / 1060 / 1200 / 1100 / 1000, h 50 (basalt) | a lava moat (a `lava` floor, glowing `[r, g, b, glow]`), basalt columns | ambient 0.55; orange lava lights along the fence; 4 light towers | ash | minor drums, saw bass |\n| **Tranquility Dome** | Meteors | lunar night: the `space` preset, a big Earth disc, the dome's ribs drawn as arcs | 1350 / 1450 / 1550 / 1450 / 1350, h 60 | regolith with craters, habitat modules, antennas, a rover | ambient 0.55; cold blue-white floods | none (\"no air, no wind, no excuses\") | spacey arpeggios |\n| **Boneyard Ballpark** | Haunts | midnight: a full moon and fog layers | 1000 / 1080 / 1120 / 1080 / 1000, h 36 (an iron cemetery fence) | tombstones, crypts, dead trees, lanterns, candles | ambient 0.45; green and blue lanterns; jack-o'-lantern glow | `leaves` weather, plus fog as Backdrop `fog` layers | spooky organ, theremin |\n| **MegaMax MegaDome** | Mechanicals | neon night: the `city-night` preset seen through the dome's glass ribs, holo-billboards | 1000 / 1060 / 1100 / 1060 / 1000, h 40; the **Mega Wall** in left (θ −45° to −20°) is h 90 | a neon concourse floor (cyan grid lines), the luxury box, drones | ambient 0.6; magenta and cyan neon lights; the MEGA-TRON's glow | none (indoors) | synthwave |\n\n**Per-park physics** (in the park def): `gravityMul` (moon 0.55), `evMul` (moon 0.8), `jumpMul` (moon 2.0), `bounceMul`\n(dome turf 1.1), and the outfielders' depth shift (moon +200 U). **Floor materials:** grass with the park's mow pattern\n(Kernel stripes, Barnacle checkerboard, Caldera dark burnt grass, Tranquility bright astroturf, Boneyard dead brown-green,\nMegaDome turf with cyan neon lines).\n\n### 7.3 Pitch catalog (`11-pitch.js` data)\n\nThe heater's base speed is 340 U/s. Break is in U at the plate (+x is toward the glove side for a right-handed\npitcher); k is the lateness exponent.\n\n| Pitch | Speed × | Break x, z | k | Special |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Heater (fastball) | 1.00 | 0, +1.5 | 1.0 | a little \"rise\" |\n| Curve (\"Uncle Charlie\") | 0.74 | +7, −10 | 2.2 | |\n| Slider | 0.86 | +9, −3 | 2.0 | |\n| Changeup (\"the Pillow\") | 0.66 | −3, −6 | 1.6 | |\n| Sinker | 0.92 | −4, −6 | 1.8 | |\n| Knuckler | 0.60 | 0, −3 | – | wobble: noise of amplitude 4 at 3 Hz from the pitch's own seed |\n| *Signatures* | | | | Butterfly Knuckler (knuckler ×1.6 wobble, it flutters), Riptide Curve, Magma Sinker, Zero-G Floater, Phantom Forkball, Gigavolt Heater (§7.1) |\n| *Team supers* | ×1.35 unless stated | | | Corn Popper, Tidal Wave, Meteor Heater, Black Hole Ball, Banshee Ball, Overclock Laser (§7.1) |\n| Pitch-O-Matic (Derby) | 0.80 | small random breaks from `rng.deal` | – | 80% in the zone; every 5th is a Golden Ball |\n\nRepertoires: Ike (heater, curve, knuckler, Butterfly); Kid Kernel (heater, slider, changeup, signature = a 1.15×\n\"Kernel Cannon\" heater); each rival ace (heater, curve or slider, changeup or sinker, signature); relievers (heater,\nslider, changeup, the team's signature).\n\n### 7.4 Supers\n\nThe supers are specified in §6.7; each team's super pitch is in §7.1. **Everyone shares** the Batzooka swing (the\nComets' bat is \"the original\"; rivals have knock-offs drawn in their team colors: the \"Krakenzooka\", \"Lavazooka\",\n\"Lunazooka\", \"Ghoulzooka\" and \"MEGAZOOKA 9000\"), Laser Arm and Afterburners.\n\n### 7.5 The Tour: story and cutscenes (`52-story.js`)\n\n**The story.** Kernel Field, home of the Comets since forever, is about to become a parking lot. Mortimer Megamax bets\nthe deed on the Kaboom Cup, a barnstorming tour of the wildest parks in baseball. The Comets' secret weapon is\nGrandma Delgado's homemade Batzooka, which only fires when the crowd roars. Each stop is a cutscene (in the Broadcast\nCam, with rigs, poses and dialog portraits), then the game (with scripted radio lines when its hazard first shows),\nthen a post-game scene.\n\n**Prologue: \"Last Game at Kernel Field?\"** (Kernel Field at dusk, after a practice)\n- HAP: \"Good evening, baseball fans, from Kernel Field, where the corn is high and the stakes are higher!\"\n- *A limousine rolls up the foul line. A bulldozer follows it.*\n- MORTIMER: \"Enjoy your little cornfield, Comets. Monday it's a parking lot. Premium spaces only.\"\n- DOT: \"Over my dead batting glove.\"\n- MORTIMER: \"Win the Kaboom Cup and I'll tear up the deed. Lose, and I pave the park AND hang that bat in my lobby.\"\n- IKE: *(opens a dusty crate)* \"Your grandma's BATZOOKA. Hickory, duct tape and a surplus bottle rocket. Summer of '62.\"\n- DOT: \"What does it do?\"\n- IKE: \"Nothin'. Till the crowd gets loud. Then it does EVERYTHING.\"\n- LOU: \"Folks, I haven't seen a bat that dangerous since I swung at my own shadow in '79!\"\n- → Offer Spring Training (\"Learn the ropes with Grandpa Ike?\" PLAY · SKIP), then the Tour Map.\n\n**Stop 1: Barnacle Bay Park vs the Krakens.**\n- *Pregame:* BRINE: \"Ahoy, corn-pickers! The tide's coming in, and it's bringing a whole ocean of hurt!\" DOT: \"We\n  brought sunscreen.\" LOU: \"Watch the gulls, folks. They've got better hands than my old infield.\"\n- *First gull snatch:* HAP: \"A seagull just stole a fly ball! Is that legal? Barb says it's... in play!\"\n- *Win:* BRINE: \"Blast it all. Take this. Barnacle Grip Tape. Sticks to anything, except a lead.\" (Lumber +1.)\n- *Loss:* BRINE: \"Back to the shallow end, landlubbers!\"\n\n**Stop 2: Caldera Field vs the Eruptors.**\n- *Pregame:* IGGY: \"Hope you packed sunscreen. SPF one million.\" IKE: \"Don't stand on anything that's glowing.\"\n- *First vent:* HAP: \"The ground just sneezed lava, and the baseball went with it!\"\n- *Scripted Rhubarb* (the first time Iggy hits a batter, or in the 2nd inning by script): LOU: \"Uh-oh, the benches\n  are emptying! Somebody fetch a fire extinguisher and a referee!\" BARB (after): \"Everybody back in your dugouts\n  before I eject the volcano!\"\n- *Win:* IGGY: \"You've got fire, Delgado. Here. Magma Cleats. They're only a little bit on fire.\" (Jet Cleats +1.)\n\n**Stop 3: Tranquility Dome vs the Meteors.**\n- *Pregame:* COSMO: \"Welcome to the Moon, Comets. Up here every pop fly is a field trip.\" HANK: \"Is there a snack bar\n  on the Moon?\" LOU: \"Gravity took the day off, folks. Somebody tell the baseball.\"\n- *First meteor shower:* HAP: \"Meteor shower in left field! The grounds crew is going to need a bigger rake!\"\n- *Win:* COSMO: \"Mission accomplished, for you. Zero-G Gloves. They catch whatever gravity drops.\" (Glue Gloves +1.)\n\n**Stop 4: Boneyard Ballpark vs the Haunts.**\n- *Pregame:* RATTLEBONES: \"We've been dying to play you. Literally. Since 1887.\" PIP: \"I'm not scared.\" PEP: \"You're\n  holding my hand.\" PIP: \"You're holding MINE.\"\n- *First Phantom Fog:* HAP: \"Where'd it go?! The ball just turned into a rumor!\"\n- *Win:* RATTLEBONES: \"A fine game, mortals. Phantom Pine Tar. It makes the crowd scream louder.\" (Hype Machine +1.)\n\n**Stop 5 (the final): the MegaMax MegaDome vs the Mechanicals, for the Kaboom Cup.**\n- *Pregame:* MORTIMER (on the MEGA-TRON): \"Meet my ace. Ninety thousand horsepower. Zero feelings. ENFORCER-9000!\"\n  ENFORCER: \"PREPARE. TO. BE. STRUCK. OUT.\" DOT: \"Then let's give him some feelings.\" IKE: \"Swing when they roar,\n  kid.\"\n- *First short circuit:* LOU: \"He's smoking! I mean really smoking! Somebody unplug that fella!\"\n- *Rally Cap* (if trailing in the last inning): HAP: \"Listen to this! The Krakens, the Eruptors, the Meteors, even\n  the Haunts! They're ALL chanting for the Comets!\" (meter → 100)\n- *Win, the ending:*\n  1. The Batzooka's last moonshot hits the MEGA-TRON, which rains sparks.\n  2. MORTIMER: \"My jumbotron! My deed! My... reputation!\"\n  3. The deed flutters into the Batzooka's backblast and burns to confetti.\n  4. DOT: \"Kernel Field stays. Same time next season?\"\n  5. ENFORCER: \"...I. LIKE. BASEBALL.\"\n  6. **Credits** roll over a blooper reel: rigs doing pratfalls, Hank eating, the mascot race tumble. Then \"THE END?\n     Exhibition: everything unlocked.\"\n- *Loss:* MORTIMER: \"Pave it! Pave it all!\" → RAIN CHECK.\n\n### 7.6 Spring Training lessons (`53-lessons.js`)\n\nEach lesson: Ike's intro (two lines), a drill with an on-screen goal (\"3 / 3 FAIR BALLS\"), prompts, and \"LESSON\nPASSED!\". Lessons 1–2 have slow motion ×0.6 on the first pitches.\n\n| # | Lesson | Drill | Passed when |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | **Batting Practice** | slow heaters from Ike; aim and time the contact swing | 3 fair balls |\n| 2 | **Power and Bunts** | power swings at meatballs, then bunt | 1 home run with a power swing and 1 fair bunt |\n| 3 | **Reading the Zone** | a mix of strikes and balls, curves included | take 2 balls and hit 2 strikes |\n| 4 | **On the Mound** | you pitch to a CPU batter | 3 strikes with 3 different pitches, one PERFECT release, one aftertouch |\n| 5 | **Leather and Lasers** | fielding: Ike hits flies and grounders | 2 fly catches, a grounder thrown to first in time, a double play |\n| 6 | **Wheels** | baserunning | advance on a hit, tag up on a fly, steal second, use turbo, slide in safe |\n| 7 | **BATZOOKA!** | the meter is pre-filled | hit a Batzooka home run, throw a super pitch, make a Laser Arm throw |\n| 8 | **Rhubarb 101** | a practice brawl with the grounds crew | land 5 punches, 1 shove and 1 toss |\n| – | **House Rules** card | what you can't do (§6.1) | – |\n\n### 7.7 Derby\n\nRules are in §6.18. Targets by park: the blimp (every park but the moon dome, which has a satellite instead), the\njumbotron or scoreboard, the bullseye on the batter's eye, and drones at the MegaDome. The hub round uses the\nMegaDome.\n\n### 7.8 Clubhouse upgrades (`55-upgrades.js`)\n\n| Upgrade | Per tier | Costs (FB) for tiers 1 / 2 / 3 |\n|---|---|---|\n| Lumber | exit speed +5% | 400 / 800 / 1400 |\n| Glue Gloves | catch radius +1 U, catch chance +2% | 300 / 700 / 1200 |\n| Jet Cleats | run and field speed +4% | 300 / 700 / 1200 |\n| Cannon Arms | throws +5%, pitch speed +3% | 400 / 800 / 1400 |\n| Hype Machine | meter gain +10% | 500 / 1000 / 1600 |\n\nThe clubhouse screen is five big cards with a picture, the tier pips, the cost and \"✕ BUY\". Grandpa Ike comments on\neach purchase.\n\n### 7.9 Commentary line pools (`54-lines.js`)\n\nAt least 6 lines per tag (and 10 for the most common: strike, ball, foul, single, out). Samples in the voice to\nmatch:\n\n| Tag | Samples |\n|---|---|\n| `batter_up` (PA) | \"Now batting... number seven... DOT... DYNAMITE... DELGADO!\" |\n| `strike_called` | \"Strike one, right on the black. You could hang a picture on that one.\" |\n| `strike_swinging` | \"Swing and a miss! He swung so hard he unscrewed himself from the box!\" |\n| `ball` | \"Ball, low. That one was dragging its feet.\" |\n| `foul_back` | \"Fouled straight back! Duck, Lou!\" / LOU: \"I've been ducking since '79.\" |\n| `strikeout` | \"Strike three! Back to the dugout to think about what he's done.\" |\n| `walk` | \"Ball four. Take your base, and take a sandwich while you're at it.\" |\n| `single` | \"Seeing-eye single through the right side! That ball had a map and a flashlight.\" |\n| `double` | \"Into the gap! {batter} is digging for second like there's buried treasure!\" |\n| `triple` | \"Off the wall, he's rounding second, he's going for three! He's SAFE!\" |\n| `homer` | \"Swung on and BELTED! Deep! Way back! That ball has left the zip code!\" / \"{dist} feet! They'll need a passport to bring that one back!\" |\n| `batzooka_ready` | \"The crowd is ROARING! You know what that means... it's BATZOOKA TIME!\" |\n| `batzooka_hit` | \"KA-BLAMMO! That's not a home run, that's a space program!\" |\n| `batzooka_fizzle` | \"Fizzle! That's the loudest nothing I've ever heard.\" |\n| `super_pitch` | \"{pitcher} just threw a pitch that's probably illegal in three states!\" |\n| `catch_dive` | \"Laid out like a welcome mat! What a grab!\" |\n| `robbery` | \"He climbed the wall and STOLE it! Call the sheriff!\" |\n| `error` | \"Clank! You could hear that one in the next county.\" |\n| `double_play` | \"Two for the price of one! Around the horn and back for a nap!\" |\n| `steal_safe` | \"He's stealing! ...SAFE! Lock up your valuables, folks.\" |\n| `bowl_over` | \"COLLISION AT THE PLATE! Somebody check the catcher's warranty!\" |\n| `rhubarb_start` | \"Here come the benches! It's a rhubarb, folks, a genuine dust-up!\" |\n| `rhubarb_end` | \"Barb's breaking it up. Everybody's dusting off. Nobody's going home, though everybody's going home dirty.\" |\n| `walkoff` | \"WALK-OFF! The {team} win it! Pile on, pile on!\" (only a home team can walk off; in the Tour the Comets are always the visitors) |\n| `lead_change` | \"And just like that, we've got ourselves a brand-new ballgame!\" |\n| `hazard_*` | one pool per park (§7.5's first-time lines plus 5 more each) |\n| `between` | \"Time for the Mascot Race! My money's on the popcorn.\" |\n| `umpire` (stamps + voice) | \"STEE-RIIIKE!\" \"BALL!\" \"YER OUT!\" \"SAFE!\" \"FAIR BALL!\" \"FOUL!\" \"PLAY BALL!\" \"TIME!\" |\n| `vendor` | \"PEANUTS!\" \"GET YER DOGS!\" \"COLD LEMONADE!\" |\n\n### 7.10 Music\n\nThe list is in §6.16. Every song is written in the engine's notation in `56-songs.js` (a melody, bass and drums at\nleast; organ voicing for the ballpark tunes; named layers for in-game loops).\n\n### 7.11 Attract reel segments (`35-attract.js`)\n\n| # | Segment (caption) | Park | What's forced | ≈ s |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | \"PLAY BALL!\" | Kernel Field | the title flyover, then a pitch duel in the Plate Cam: a called strike, a foul back, then a line-drive single and the throw in | 18 |\n| 2 | \"SUPER PITCHES\" | Caldera | Iggy's Meteor Heater for a swinging strike three; then a fly ball launched by a lava vent | 15 |\n| 3 | \"LEATHER AND LASERS\" | Barnacle Bay | a diving catch in right; a gull snatches a fly; a Laser Arm throw home, a slide and a bowl-over | 20 |\n| 4 | \"WHEELS\" | Kernel Field | a steal of second with a headfirst dive; turbo | 12 |\n| 5 | \"BATZOOKA!\" | MegaDome | Dot arms the Batzooka: the moonshot, the Moonshot Cam, the MEGA-TRON explodes, fireworks, the trot | 20 |\n| 6 | \"RHUBARB!\" | Caldera | HBP into the brawl: fight clouds; Barb breaks it up | 14 |\n| 7 | \"SIX WILD PARKS\" | Tranquility | a low-gravity fly; the CF climbs the wall 3× high for a robbery | 14 |\n| 8 | (continued) | Boneyard | the Banshee Ball (an invisible pitch) for a whiff; a ghost wall catch | 14 |\n| 9 | \"1–4 PLAYERS · PLAY ONLINE IN AI HUB\" | MegaDome | Derby swings with three ghost comets (local fakes) | 15 |\n| 10 | \"MOONSHOT LEADERS\" | – | the high-score table, then the title logo and \"PRESS START\" | 10 |\n\n### 7.12 Art assets to make (`04-shapes.js`, code-drawn sprites)\n\nUse the engine's core library where it fits (`barrel`, `crate`, `bench`, `fence`, `tree`, `pine`, `rock`, `bush`,\n`lamppost`, `sign`, `cart`, `table`) and props (`lamp`, `streetlamp`, `banner`, `torch`, `brazier`, `firedrum`, `candle`,\n`lantern`, `pot`, `skull`, `cobweb`). Write new `E.SHAPES` entries (check each with `node tools/asset-sheet.mjs`) for:\n- **Every park:** the base (a white pillow), home plate, the rubber, the mound, the foul pole, the dugout bench, the\n  bat rack, the helmet rack, the water cooler, the rosin bag, a light tower (with `lights:`), a scoreboard frame, the\n  jumbotron frame, the batting-practice L-screen, the batting cage net, the Pitch-O-Matic 3000.\n- **Kernel Field:** cornstalk, silo, hay bale, red-barn scoreboard, windmill, windsock.\n- **Barnacle Bay:** lighthouse, boat, buoy, pier piling, lobster trap.\n- **Caldera:** basalt column, lava vent (cone, with glow), warning sign.\n- **Tranquility:** habitat module, antenna, satellite dish, rover, airlock.\n- **Boneyard:** tombstone (3 shapes by seed), crypt, iron fence section, jack-o'-lantern.\n- **MegaDome:** holo-billboard, drone, luxury box, MEGA-TRON.\n\n**Code-drawn sprites:** the ball (5×5, with stitches, 2 rotating frames), the blimp, gulls (a Blob with wings), the\nlanding marker, the reticles (contact: a thin ring; power: a thick red ring; Batzooka: a ring of fire), the pitch\ntarget and release ring, the zone grid, base rings, the glyph icons (§6.13), the meter gauges, the scorebug, the\nBatzooka overdraw (nozzle, fins and a glowing barrel over the bat in the hands), the fight cloud, popcorn, confetti\nand fireworks.\n\n---\n\n## 8. Art and animation\n\n### 8.1 Look (the engine's own look target, applied)\n\nTASK.md puts frame-rate targets and optimization out of scope, so add as much detail as each scene needs: big\ncrowds, many lights, particles, shadows and props.\n\n1. **Resolution:** `res: 'ps1'`, `expand: true`. The HUD anchors to `r.W` and `r.H`. Rigs are `size: 1.15–1.35`\n   (bosses 2.2); props use `propSize: 1.3`.\n2. **Dressed characters:** every player gets the team uniform, plus hair, skin, build and size of their own, and the\n   gear for their job (below). Nobody keeps the defaults.\n3. **Backdrops:** every park's sky is an `E.Backdrop` (§7.2), seen in the Plate Cam and the Moonshot Cam. The Broadcast\n   Cam shows ground to the screen's edges (the park continues past the stands; `map.outside` is the park's ground\n   color).\n4. **Textures:** grass with grain and a mow pattern, dirt with speckle, chalk lines slightly worn, the warning track,\n   padded fence faces, stone or plank stands.\n5. **Props on every screen:** dugouts, bat racks, coolers, light towers, poles, the park's own pieces (§7.12), 3–8 in\n   any Broadcast Cam view.\n6. **Effects on every hit** (§8.4).\n7. **Color:** everything drawn by hand is shaded with `E.tones` and `E.ramp`.\n8. **Type:** the `E.font.title` logo and stamps; HUD text with shadows; `E.ui.box` gradient panels.\n9. **Light:** night parks run `game.lights` with tower floods and local glows; day parks a warm high ambient.\n   Emissive for fire, neon, lasers and the Batzooka.\n10. **Faces in dialog:** every speaker has a live portrait (`rig.drawPortrait`), the announcers included.\n\n### 8.2 Rigs and uniforms (`03-rigs.js`)\n\n`BZ.makeRig(player, team, job)` builds an `E.Humanoid` from the team's colors and the player's looks:\n\n| Job | Kit |\n|---|---|\n| batter | `hat: 'batting'` in the team color, `weapon: 'bat'`, `grip: 'both'`, batting gloves (`colors.glove`) |\n| fielder | `hat: 'cap'`, `mitt: 'fielder'` (`'first'` for 1B) |\n| catcher | `hat: 'mask'`, `armor: true` (the chest protector, `plate` = the team's dark color), `mitt: 'catcher'` |\n| pitcher | `hat: 'cap'`, `mitt: 'fielder'` |\n| runner | `hat: 'batting'`, no bat |\n| umpire | `outfit: 'coat'` (navy), `hat: 'mask'` |\n| robots | metal colors, `eyeGlow`, a stiffer gait (`stride` and `swing` lower), sparks when short-circuited |\n| skeletons | `build: 'skeleton'`, `colors.bone` |\n| mascots, gulls, ghosts, drones | `E.Blob` (`feet`, `wings`, `mouth`, `face: 'front'`) |\n\nRigs are cached per player and job and swapped as the job changes (batter → runner → fielder between halves).\n\n### 8.3 New animations\n\n**Motion clips.** One set file, `assets/mocap-batzooka.js`:\n```\nnode tools/anim-set.mjs <repo>/src/mocap/sets/quaternius.js <repo>/examples/cmu-lib/CMU_124.js <repo>/src/mocap/sets/mesh2motion.js \\\n  --clips 124_01,124_07,124_08,124_12,QUATERNIUS:Slide_Start,QUATERNIUS:Slide_Loop,QUATERNIUS:Slide_Exit,QUATERNIUS:Punch_Jab,QUATERNIUS:Punch_Cross,Victory,Cheering_Two_Hands \\\n  --name BATZOOKA --out assets/mocap-batzooka.js\n```\nIf a clip name is reported as in two sets, prefix it with `SET:`, as the tool asks. Load `engine/mocap-readable.js`,\n`engine/mocap.js` and the set after the engine. Then:\n- `const lib = Mocap.load(MOCAP.BATZOOKA)`, and `Mocap.drive(rig, lib)` once per rig that uses clips.\n- The CMU takes are long, with several repetitions. Write `tools/clip-windows.mjs` to find one clean window per motion\n  (the hands' speed peak marks contact or release; the window runs from the last still moment before it to the next\n  one after it) and store them as data: `{ swing: ['124_07', a, b, contactAt], pitch: ['124_01', a, b, releaseAt], ... }`.\n- Time-map each window so that its contact or release key lands exactly on the game's moment (the swing delay, the\n  release time).\n- `rig.mocapW` fades in and out over 0.08 s. Lefties use `MocapReadable.mirror(clip)`, made once at load.\n- The bat follows the hands (`rig.mocapBlade = true`, with the `bat` weapon drawn along the knuckle line).\n- Review every motion with `tools/filmstrip.mjs` on the `#gallery` page. If a clip reads badly at game size, use the\n  procedural fallback in the table (both are written, and the better one is picked by looking at the strips).\n\n| Motion | Source | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| batting stance and waggle | procedural: the bat up and back, knees bent (`crouch` .3), the bat bobbing on a sine with a per-player tempo | |\n| contact swing | clip 124_07 window, time-mapped to 0.10 s to the plane | fallback spec `SWING`: `{ rel: true, hand: 'both', a0: 2.4, a1: −2.6, z0: −2, z1: −4, reach: 6, wind: .10, active: .08, recover: .30, lunge: 2.2, twist: 2.2, lean: .25, hold: .35 }` |\n| power swing | the same window, stretched to 0.14 s, with a bigger stride (root forward 3 U) | fallback: `SWING` with lunge 3, twist 2.8 |\n| Batzooka swing | the power swing plus a recoil hop (`rig.kick`), muzzle flash and smoke | |\n| bunt | clip 124_08 window | fallback: the bat held level at the chest with both hands (an IK override) |\n| windup and pitch | clip 124_01 window (set, leg lift, stride, release, follow-through); mirrored for lefties; the ball leaves `rig.hand()` at the release key | fallback: the `knee` kick spec (leg lift) chained into `throw` (lunge 2.4, lean .6) |\n| underhand toss (Ike's batting practice, Derby intro) | clip 124_12 | |\n| fielder's throw | `E.MOVES.throw` plus a crow-hop for outfielders (`hop: .8`) | |\n| catch high, low and backhand | procedural: after `solvePose`, IK the glove hand to the ball (`E.ik3`); the body turns to it | |\n| dive | procedural: lean forward and blend `down` 0→1 over 0.2 s while the body slides; the glove reaches out | |\n| jump catch | `Body.jump` plus `air: true` and the glove IK'd up | |\n| wall climb | `climb: true` with vz (hand-over-hand) facing the fence; a reach at the top | |\n| feet-first slide | clips Slide_Start → Slide_Loop → Slide_Exit | |\n| headfirst dive | procedural: `down` blend, forward lean, both arms out | |\n| run and turbo | the engine's gait from velocity; turbo uses `sprint: true` (lean) plus speed lines | |\n| tag | a low swipe with the glove hand (custom spec, `hand: 'L'`) | |\n| umpire calls | strike: a right-fist punch-out (`cross` with a long `hold`) and `expr: 'shout'`; out: a fist pump (`uppercut`); safe: both arms sweeping out wide (a two-hand spec: a0 1.4 → a1 −0.2) | |\n| celebrations | clips Victory and Cheering_Two_Hands; `pose: 'cheer'`; high-fives (two rigs meeting); the dugout bounce | |\n| dejection | `pose: 'kneel'`, `expr: 'wince'` | |\n| Rhubarb | `E.Combo(['jab', 'cross', 'hook'])` (or clips Punch_Jab and Punch_Cross), `bash`, `throw`, `down` with dizzy stars | |\n| catcher | the `crouch` pose; the mitt IK'd to the pitch; popping up to throw | |\n| walk-up | walking with the bat on the shoulder; two practice swings | |\n| the trot | a jog; high-fives with the base coaches; a cap tip | |\n\n### 8.4 Effects\n\n- **Contact:** sparks and a ring by Q, a white flash 0.06 s, hit-stop 0.06 s, rumble.\n- **Broken bat:** on jammed contact (Q < 0.15 against a heater at 1.0× or more, 8% chance from `rng.fx`; cosmetic\n  only), wood splinters (`particles.bits` in wood colors) and \"CRACK! Broken bat!\" on the radio.\n- **Pitch trails:** speed lines for heaters; fire for the Meteor Heater; a wave sprite for the Tidal Wave; a dark\n  swirl for the Black Hole; a shimmer while invisible; a laser line for the Overclock Laser (emissive); popcorn puffs\n  for the Corn Popper.\n- **Ball:** a trail above 500 U/s; dust on bounces; sparks off the fence; a splash in water; a lava sizzle; a meteor\n  crater decal.\n- **Players:** dust on slides and dives; speed lines on turbo; fire trails for Afterburners; stars and a ring on\n  collisions; dizzy stars.\n- **Spectacle:** fireworks (`particles.explosion` small, plus colored sparks), confetti, popcorn, the crowd wave,\n  scoreboard bulbs, the jumbotron, heat shimmer at Caldera.\n- **Comfort:** every `shake` and `flash` follows the comfort settings.\n\n---\n\n## 9. Build order and milestones\n\nBuild in this order. Each milestone ends with its tests passing (`node tests/run.mjs`), the bundle building, and a\nplayable build. Temporary scaffolding inside a milestone is fine, but nothing temporary survives M8.\n\n**M0: Foundation.**\n- Make the dev folder (§4.1) and fetch the sources (§3.1).\n- `npm install`, then `npx playwright install chromium`. If `/tmp` is full on this shared machine (it was while","numLines":420,"startLine":1380,"totalLines":2144}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_013jZTU48ic8VoiKEx1WkZvX","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cghvz77NPu81BNh8eeE6j","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_019Wd6cPcNg85NKof9kdPNpJ","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium.build__20261104-060114__x4549c1/work/PLAN.md","offset":1800,"limit":345},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":16258,"cache_read_input_tokens":70869,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":16258},"output_tokens":16,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a605ca8e-6f21-4c44-bd74-b97a2b38e121","uuid":"04fef48f-96cd-4f28-92dd-d2c0bbdc3902","timestamp":"2026-11-04T13:01:37.731Z","request_id":"req_011Cghvz6pkLiK9RsCWSPP7C","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_019Wd6cPcNg85NKof9kdPNpJ":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium.build__20261104-060114__x4549c1/work/PLAN.md","offset":1800,"limit":345}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019Wd6cPcNg85NKof9kdPNpJ","type":"tool_result","content":"1800\t  planning), run Playwright and Chromium with `TMPDIR=<dev>/.tmp`.\n1801\t- Write `tools/build.mjs` (concat `src/` into `build/game.js`; bundle `../BatzookaBaseball-Baseball-claude-opus-5-5-max-20261103-174819.html` per §12).\n1802\t- Write `tests/run.mjs` and the headless loader (§11.2); `index.html`; the `00-core` spine (registries, bus, RNG,\n1803\t  TUNE); the boot, title and match scene skeletons; the `game.debug` skeleton.\n1804\t- Make engine changes 1, 2, 4 and 5 (§3.3), and a first `#gallery` scene (rigs on a plain field) to look at the bat and\n1805\t  mitt; the full gallery comes with dev mode in M5.\n1806\t- **Done when:** the bundle opens to a title in `tools/check.mjs` with no errors, the smoke test passes, and the\n1807\t  gallery shows a rig holding a bat and wearing a mitt.\n1808\t\n1809\t**M1: The at-bat** (the core, and the biggest risk; §10 R1 and R2).\n1810\t- Field geometry and the Kernel Field TileMap; the Plate Cam with the fence, stands and towers.\n1811\t- The pitcher, batter and catcher rigs with clips or fallbacks.\n1812\t- Pitch types, windup, release ring, aftertouch; the reticle, swings and contact model; the count rules and calls.\n1813\t- Batted-ball physics with home run, foul and fair detection; the Broadcast Cam showing the ball's flight.\n1814\t- Umpire stamps, basic sounds, the timing feedback and the dev timing bar.\n1815\t- For this milestone only, a ball in play resolves at its landing as a \"HIT!\" or \"OUT!\" stamp by a simple rule. M3\n1816\t  replaces this with real fielding.\n1817\t- **Done when:** T-PITCH, T-BAT, T-BALL and T-RULES (the count part) pass; 200 bot at-bats against the CPU give a\n1818\t  sensible spread (whiffs, fouls, grounders, flies, line drives and some home runs, from the contact readouts); Plate Cam\n1819\t  screenshots at 1280×720 and 1920×1080 show a readable zone, batter, pitcher and ball.\n1820\t\n1821\t**M2: The Derby and the AI Hub** (early, to settle the protocol and the bundle; §10 R7 and R8).\n1822\t- The Derby: local play with 1–4 players hot seat, targets, scoring, the initials table.\n1823\t- `40-hub.js`: connect, our card, ready, start, progress, result, time-up, end, ghosts.\n1824\t- The session rules, the meta tags, and the session client placement in the bundle.\n1825\t- **Done when:** T-DERBY and T-HUB pass headless, and `window.__hubCheck.pass` is true in the real harness for\n1826\t  `players=2&auto=1`, `players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1` and `&scenario=host-leave`; the bundle still opens normally outside\n1827\t  a hub.\n1828\t\n1829\t**M3: Fielding, running and the full game.**\n1830\t- Fielders (assignment, chase, catch, throw, cutoffs, tags, forces, rundowns); baserunners (forces, tag-ups, orders,\n1831\t  steals, pickoffs, slides).\n1832\t- The full rules engine (innings, end of game, extra innings, mercy, errors).\n1833\t- The human fielding and running controls, mouse included; the CPU brains; line scores and the results screen.\n1834\t- **Done when:** T-RULES, T-FIELD, T-RUN and T-AI pass (CPU vs CPU sims in range), and a 3-inning game with the bot\n1835\t  as player 1 (through the real controls) against the CPU plays from start to finish with no stuck play.\n1836\t\n1837\t**M4: The over-the-top layer.**\n1838\t- The meter and all supers; turbo; dive, jump and wall climb; headfirst dives; the bowl-over.\n1839\t- The Moonshot Cam, fireworks and the trot; replays; the crowd, hype and the wave; the jumbotron; mascots;\n1840\t  between-innings shows; the Rhubarb.\n1841\t- The commentary director with the babble voices; all music and sound effects.\n1842\t- **Done when:** T-SUPER, T-RHU, T-CAM, T-TALK, T-AUD and T-CROWD pass, and filmstrips of the swing, pitch, dive,\n1843\t  slide, wall climb, umpire calls and Rhubarb punches look clean (wind-up, strike, settle).\n1844\t\n1845\t**M5: The front end, input polish, dev mode and saves.**\n1846\t- Title (with its mode menu), Team Select with joining (1–4), results, Playbook, the pause items, About/Credits (with\n1847\t  provisional feedback text, rewritten in M8).\n1848\t- Our settings; the glyph renderer and prompts (PlayStation by default, Xbox by setting, keyboard, mouse); mouse\n1849\t  hover and clicks on every screen and in the world.\n1850\t- The touch-only card; dev mode (all six tabs, pinned sliders, the gallery); saves.\n1851\t- **Done when:** T-UI, T-IN, T-HUD, T-DEV, T-MP and T-TOUCH pass, and screenshots of the prompts for a PlayStation pad,\n1852\t  an Xbox setting, the keyboard and the mouse look right.\n1853\t\n1854\t**M6: Content.**\n1855\t- All six teams and rosters with the captains' signatures and team supers; the six parks with their looks, lights and\n1856\t  hazards; the boss rules.\n1857\t- The Tour (map, clubhouse, rewards, every cutscene, the ending and credits roll); Spring Training's eight lessons.\n1858\t- All line pools.\n1859\t- **Done when:** T-HAZ, T-TOUR and T-TRAIN pass, the playthrough test passes, and screenshots of every park in both\n1860\t  main cameras look like their descriptions.\n1861\t\n1862\t**M7: The attract mode.**\n1863\t- The director and the ten segments, the idle detection, exiting on input, touch-only compatibility.\n1864\t- **Done when:** T-ATT passes and a filmed loop (screenshots every 10 s across one loop) shows every segment.\n1865\t\n1866\t**M8: Polish, verify and ship.**\n1867\t- **Balance:** sims and slider sessions; then write the tuned defaults into `TUNE` (the \"reset to defaults\" values).\n1868\t- **Look:** act on every `check.mjs` look note; check every park and screen at TV size.\n1869\t- **Animation:** a filmstrip pass.\n1870\t- **Writing:** a pass over every line for tone, length and repetition.\n1871\t- **Feedback:** write the final About text and the four feedback sections.\n1872\t- **Ship:** grep for leftovers (§12); `exit-interview.json`; the final bundle; every test, the browser checks and the\n1873\t  hub harness green.\n1874\t\n1875\t---\n1876\t\n1877\t## 10. Risks and how to take them down\n1878\t\n1879\t| # | Risk | Why it is risky | De-risk early | Fallback |\n1880\t|---|---|---|---|---|\n1881\t| R1 | The Plate Cam (Mode 7) doesn't read: the batter hides the zone, near rigs look odd, walls sort wrong | Mode 7's billboards are mostly used for karts, not near-camera people | Prototype on day one of M1, with screenshots at both box sides; every camera number in TUNE; the batter offset to the side, the camera shifted 4 U the other way; the catcher at 85% opacity | A custom low `E.View` (pitch 18) from behind the plate, with the ball's size scaled by its distance and drawn by hand (an orthographic view) |\n1882\t| R2 | Batting isn't fun or fair | Timing, aim and outcome must feel causal | A deterministic pitch path with a known crossing; the dev timing bar and contact readout; timing feedback text; unit tests of the contact mapping; sims of outcome rates; assists by difficulty | Widen the windows and sweet spot by TUNE; an aim assist that pulls the reticle 30% toward the ball |\n1883\t| R3 | Rules edge cases (forces, tag-ups, third-out timing) | Baseball's rules are subtle | A pure rules module with a table-driven test of 24+ situations; explicit lists of kept and dropped rules | Simplify the case (for example, auto-return runners on caught flies) and say so in House Rules |\n1884\t| R4 | Fielding AI looks dumb: two fielders on one ball, nobody covering | Roles depend on the situation | A role table by ball direction and runners; a test of coverage in each situation; one chaser at a time | Auto-assign the cover men by the nearest open base |\n1885\t| R5 | Fly balls leave the screen in the Broadcast Cam | High apexes | The display height squash, the landing marker, `cam.frame` zooming out to 0.5 | A small picture-in-picture \"ball cam\" in a corner showing the ball against the sky |\n1886\t| R6 | Mocap clips fit badly (the bat's direction, long takes, mirroring) | CMU takes are raw | The window finder; review in the gallery with filmstrips; procedural fallbacks already written | Use the procedural moves for that motion |\n1887\t| R7 | The hub protocol fails in the single file | Ordering of scripts, the card, cadence | Build it in M2, run the real harness then and keep it in `--hub`; the mock in headless tests; follow §6.21 to the letter | Parallel mode (drop the ghost traffic and change one meta), if ghosts are the failing check |\n1888\t| R8 | The bundle breaks: `</script>` inside inlined code, an external request, the file:// origin | Inlining 1.3 MB of code | The build scans for `</script` and `<!--` in the inlined code and fails if it finds them; `check.mjs` lists external requests (there must be none); test both file:// and served | Split the inlined code into several `<script>` blocks |\n1889\t| R9 | PlayStation symbols missing from the font | The 5×7 font is ASCII plus a few symbols | The icon renderer, plus the four glyphs added to the font; T-HUD checks every label | – |\n1890\t| R10 | Scope: many systems and much content | A demo with a whole Tour | Strict milestones; content as data; the playthrough test catches regressions | Quick Tour games (1 inning) by default if time runs short (the setting exists anyway) |\n1891\t| R11 | The attract director is brittle with forced outcomes | Scripted events can miss | A time limit per segment and moving on by itself; forced outcomes through `game.debug.force` | Skip the segment and log it (a test fails if any segment is skipped) |\n1892\t| R12 | Determinism drifts (tests flake) | Cosmetic code using `Math.random` in the rules | The rng-stream rule; the proof hash twice per run (T-CORE) | – |\n1893\t| R13 | The shared machine: a full `/tmp`, ports, other agents | Seen while planning | `TMPDIR` in the dev folder; the server on 127.0.0.1 with port 0; stop only your own PIDs | – |\n1894\t\n1895\t---\n1896\t\n1897\t## 11. Testing\n1898\t\n1899\t### 11.1 One command\n1900\t\n1901\t`node tests/run.mjs` (also `npm test`) runs every headless suite and prints **only failures**, then one line:\n1902\t`212 passed, 0 failed (38.4 s)`. The exit code is 1 on any failure.\n1903\t- `--browser` adds the browser checks (§11.6), `--hub` the AI Hub harness (§11.7), `--full` the long balance sims\n1904\t  (§11.5); `--all` runs everything.\n1905\t- `--only <suite>` reruns one suite. Rerun a suite only after changing the code it covers.\n1906\t- Tests and tools play the game headless and read its state. Screenshots are only for what a script can't judge: the\n1907\t  look, framing and readability.\n1908\t- Per TASK.md, no subagents or workflows debate, review, judge or audit.\n1909\t\n1910\t**The shared machine:**\n1911\t- Prefer file:// and the headless tools.\n1912\t- The hub harness needs a server: `tools/serve.mjs` binds **127.0.0.1 on port 0** and prints the port the OS picked (or\n1913\t  `python3 -m http.server 0 --bind 127.0.0.1`). Fetch the page once to confirm it is this game (its `<title>` is\n1914\t  \"Batzooka Baseball\") before trusting a result.\n1915\t- Stop only the processes you started, by their PID. Never use `pkill`, `killall`, `fuser -k`, or kill whatever holds\n1916\t  a port.\n1917\t- Don't read files outside the dev folder and this folder, apart from the sources in §3.1.\n1918\t- If `/tmp` is full, set `TMPDIR=<dev>/.tmp` for Playwright.\n1919\t\n1920\t### 11.2 The headless harness and `game.debug`\n1921\t\n1922\t`tests/lib/load.mjs` makes a `vm` context with the stand-ins the kits' test uses (`window`, `addEventListener`,\n1923\t`location`), plus `navigator`, `matchMedia` and a fake `AIHub` when asked. It runs `engine/my-3d2dge.js`, the mocap\n1924\tfiles and `build/game.js` in it, and returns `{ E, game, BZ }`.\n1925\t- Tests drive the game with `game.advance(seconds)` (exact 1/120 s steps), `game.input.tap / hold`, `addPlayer` and\n1926\t  `input.feed` (mouse), and read `game.debug.snapshot()`.\n1927\t- The bots (§6.11) play real controls.\n1928\t- A determinism check (T-CORE-03) runs the same seeded half-inning twice and compares the hash of its snapshots, then\n1929\t  once more with `Math.random` seeded differently, where the gameplay hash must not change.\n1930\t\n1931\t`game.debug` (Appendix D) has `snapshot`, `setup`, `force`, `tune`, `resetTune`, `events`, `bot`, `step`, `skip`,\n1932\t`warp` and `hubMock`.\n1933\t\n1934\t### 11.3 The test catalog\n1935\t\n1936\t| Suite | IDs | Covers |\n1937\t|---|---|---|\n1938\t| core | T-CORE-01..05 | registries; the bus; RNG streams; determinism (the same seeded half-inning twice gives the same snapshot hash, and a third run with `Math.random` seeded differently gives the same gameplay hash of score, outs, bases and ball path, which proves the rules never use `Math.random`); TUNE meta complete (every key has a label, range and default) |\n1939\t| rules | T-RULES-01..24 | §6.1 |\n1940\t| pitch | T-PITCH-01..12 | §6.2 |\n1941\t| bat | T-BAT-01..14 | §6.3 |\n1942\t| ball | T-BALL-01..12 | §6.4 |\n1943\t| field | T-FIELD-01..16 | §6.5 |\n1944\t| run | T-RUN-01..14 | §6.6 |\n1945\t| super | T-SUPER-01..10 | §6.7 |\n1946\t| rhubarb | T-RHU-01..06 | §6.9 |\n1947\t| hazards | T-HAZ-01..08 | §6.10 |\n1948\t| ai | T-AI-01..08 | §6.11 (sims in §11.5) |\n1949\t| cams | T-CAM-01..07 | §6.12 |\n1950\t| hud | T-HUD-01..08 | §6.13 |\n1951\t| input | T-IN-01..10 | §6.14 |\n1952\t| talk | T-TALK-01..07 | §6.15 |\n1953\t| audio | T-AUD-01..04 | §6.16 |\n1954\t| crowd | T-CROWD-01..04 | §6.17 |\n1955\t| modes | T-TOUR-01..06, T-TRAIN-01..08, T-DERBY-01..06 | Tour progression, rewards, clubhouse purchases change stats, save and load round-trip; each lesson's pass condition is reachable by its lesson bot; Derby outs, scoring, Golden Balls, targets, the initials table |\n1956\t| mp | T-MP-01..05 | §6.20 |\n1957\t| hub | T-HUB-01..08 | §6.21, with the mock |\n1958\t| attract | T-ATT-01..05 | §6.22 |\n1959\t| dev | T-DEV-01..06 | §6.23 |\n1960\t| ui | T-UI-01..06 | §6.24 |\n1961\t| touch | T-TOUCH-01..03 | §6.26 |\n1962\t| about | T-ABOUT-01..03 | every Source Information field present and non-empty; the four feedback sections present; the version label shows |\n1963\t| playthrough | T-PLAY-01 | §11.4 |\n1964\t\n1965\t### 11.4 The scripted playthrough of the whole game (T-PLAY-01)\n1966\t\n1967\tOne test, run by the bot through the real inputs with `BZ.cosmetic = false`, with no errors allowed anywhere\n1968\t(`game.errors` empty at every step) and a real-time limit (measure the run once, then fix the limit at about 1.5× that,\n1969\tand at most 5 minutes):\n1970\t1. Boot to the title. Idle 10.5 s: the attract mode starts. Let its whole reel loop once. A tap returns to the title.\n1971\t2. **Spring Training:** all eight lessons, by their lesson bots, each reaching \"LESSON PASSED!\".\n1972\t3. **New Tour in slot 1, with Tour game length Quick:**\n1973\t   - Prologue: advance with ✕.\n1974\t   - Each of the five stops: its pregame, its game, its postgame. In the games the player-1 bot plays at the \"Batzooka\"\n1975\t     level against a Rookie CPU, with the dev cheat \"perfect contact\" on for the bot's side only, so every stop is\n1976\t     won in bounded time.\n1977\t   - After each stop: buy one upgrade in the clubhouse; save.\n1978\t   - Check the scripted Rhubarb at Caldera, the Rally Cap or the boss's short circuit at the MegaDome, the ending and\n1979\t     the credits roll, and the return to the title.\n1980\t4. **Load slot 1** and confirm the Tour is complete and everything is unlocked.\n1981\t5. **Exhibition with four bot players** (two a side) for one inning in a random park; the results screen.\n1982\t6. **Derby** with two hot-seat bots; the initials entry.\n1983\t7. **Hub round** with the mock: card, ready, start, progress, result, end.\n1984\t8. Open the About screen and every page; open the pause menu, then Dev Mode, move a slider, reset it.\n1985\t\n1986\t### 11.5 Balance sims (part of the `ai` suite)\n1987\t\n1988\t- Seeded CPU-vs-CPU 9-inning games at Pro must land in the ranges of T-AI-01: 6 games in the default run, 30 with\n1989\t  `--full` (`M.fast = true` keeps them quick).\n1990\t- Each difficulty pairing: in the default run, the higher level must score more runs in total over 3 seeded games;\n1991\t  with `--full`, it must win at least 60% of 10.\n1992\t- A bot batter against each pitch type: the contact rate is 55–85% at Pro.\n1993\t- The Batzooka's home run rate on contact is 70–95%.\n1994\t- The mean Derby round score of the bot is 1,500–4,000 ft.\n1995\t\n1996\tThese sims only report. The defaults are tuned with them and the sliders in M8, and the ranges stay as tests.\n1997\t\n1998\t### 11.6 Browser checks (`--browser`)\n1999\t\n2000\t- `node tools/check.mjs <bundle>.html` at the default 1280×720, then with `#match`, `#derby`, `#about`, `#gallery`,\n2001\t  then `--size 1920x1080`, and `#touch --size 390x844@3` (the touch-only card). There must be no errors, no external\n2002\t  requests (the bundle is offline), and the canvas covered. Act on every look note.\n2003\t- `tools/filmstrip.mjs` strips (with `--seed 1`, so they repeat) of the swing (contact, power, Batzooka), the pitch,\n2004\t  the throw, the dive, the slide, the wall climb, the umpire calls and the Rhubarb punches. Look at each: wind-up,\n2005\t  strike and settle, with no jerks or backward sweeps.\n2006\t- **Screenshots only for what scripts can't judge.** Look at each:\n2007\t  - the Plate Cam in each park and both batter's boxes;\n2008\t  - the Broadcast Cam on a deep fly;\n2009\t  - the HUD at 1920×1080 (a TV);\n2010\t  - prompts for the pad (PlayStation and Xbox), the keyboard and the mouse;\n2011\t  - the title, Team Select, the Tour Map, the clubhouse, the results, Dev Mode, the About pages;\n2012\t  - the Moonshot Cam;\n2013\t  - each hazard;\n2014\t  - the touch-only card.\n2015\t\n2016\t### 11.7 The AI Hub harness (`--hub`)\n2017\t\n2018\t`tests/hub.mjs` (Playwright):\n2019\t1. Copy the bundle beside `hub/harness.html`, `bridge.js` and `round.js`, and start `tools/serve.mjs` (127.0.0.1,\n2020\t   port 0).\n2021\t2. Open `harness.html?game=<bundle>.html&players=2&auto=1`. Wait for `document.body.dataset.complete === 'true'`, then\n2022\t   require `window.__hubCheck.pass === true`, and print the failing checks if not.\n2023\t3. Repeat with `players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1`, and with `players=2&scenario=host-leave&auto=1`.\n2024\t4. Open the bundle alone to confirm it reaches the title outside a session.\n2025\t5. Stop the server by its PID.\n2026\t\n2027\t---\n2028\t\n2029\t## 12. Packaging and hand-off\n2030\t\n2031\t**`tools/build.mjs` writes the single file** `BatzookaBaseball-Baseball-claude-opus-5-5-max-20261103-174819.html`\n2032\tinto this folder (the dev folder's parent), from this template:\n2033\t```html\n2034\t<!doctype html>\n2035\t<html lang=\"en\">\n2036\t<head>\n2037\t<meta charset=\"utf-8\">\n2038\t<script>/* vendor/aihub-session.js, unmodified, inlined: the first script, right after meta charset */</script>\n2039\t<meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1, viewport-fit=cover\">\n2040\t<title>Batzooka Baseball</title>\n2041\t<meta name=\"description\" content=\"Over-the-top arcade baseball: fireball pitches, a rocket-powered bat, wall-climbing catches and bench-clearing rhubarbs.\">\n2042\t<!-- the hub tags of §6.21 -->\n2043\t<style>html,body{margin:0;height:100%;background:#000;overflow:hidden}#screen{width:100%;height:100%;display:block;image-rendering:pixelated;touch-action:none}</style>\n2044\t</head>\n2045\t<body>\n2046\t<!-- E.bootSplash('BATZOOKA BASEBALL') markup, as the handoff's index.html has it -->\n2047\t<canvas id=\"screen\"></canvas>\n2048\t<script>/* engine/my-3d2dge.js */</script>\n2049\t<script>/* engine/mocap-readable.js + engine/mocap.js + assets/mocap-batzooka.js */</script>\n2050\t<script>/* build/game.js */</script>\n2051\t</body>\n2052\t</html>\n2053\t```\n2054\t\n2055\t**Build rules:**\n2056\t- **Inlined code:** inline each file as is. If one contains `</script` or `<!--`, stop with an error naming the file\n2057\t  and line, and fix the source (don't escape blindly).\n2058\t- **No outside requests:** no CDN and no network; the page works from file://.\n2059\t- **Size:** the bundle is about 1.5–2 MB, which is fine.\n2060\t- **The hub client:** after building, check that the bundle's first `<script>` is the hub client, byte-identical to\n2061\t  `vendor/aihub-session.js`.\n2062\t\n2063\t**Before handing back:**\n2064\t1. Every test is green with `node tests/run.mjs --all`, including the playthrough, the browser checks and the hub\n2065\t   harness.\n2066\t2. No leftovers: `grep -rniE \"TODO|FIXME|XXX|placeholder|lorem|stub|not implemented\" src/` finds nothing, and no\n2067\t   screen, line or button says \"coming soon\".\n2068\t3. The About/Credits screen shows the final Source Information and the three feedback sections, answered honestly (the\n2069\t   number of issues testing caught, how many were critical, the most and least helpful tests; the six engine answers;\n2070\t   the four prompt answers), with \"unknown\" where something can't be confirmed.\n2071\t4. **`exit-interview.json`** sits in this folder beside the .html, in exactly TASK.md's shape, with every value filled\n2072\t   in (§6.27 for `aiHub`). It must parse:\n2073\t   `node -e \"JSON.parse(require('fs').readFileSync('exit-interview.json','utf8'))\"`.\n2074\t5. `ENGINE-CHANGES.md` is complete, and the same list is in the engine feedback.\n2075\t6. **The final chat reply** holds the Source Information, the Testing Feedback, the Engine Feedback and the Prompt\n2076\t   Feedback (as TASK.md requires), and a short summary of the game.\n2077\t\n2078\t---\n2079\t\n2080\t## Appendix A: `BZ.TUNE` defaults (the dev sliders)\n2081\t\n2082\t| Group | Key | Default | Min–max | Meaning |\n2083\t|---|---|---|---|---|\n2084\t| Pitching | `pitchSpeed` | 1.0 | 0.5–2.0 | × every pitch's speed |\n2085\t| | `pitchBreak` | 1.0 | 0–2.5 | × break |\n2086\t| | `aftertouch` | 1.0 | 0–3 | × in-flight steering |\n2087\t| | `releaseWindow` | 1.0 | 0.3–3 | × the perfect-release window |\n2088\t| | `staminaDrain` | 1.0 | 0–3 | × stamina cost |\n2089\t| Batting | `swingTiming` | 1.0 | 0.3–3 | × the timing windows |\n2090\t| | `sweetSpot` | 1.0 | 0.4–2.5 | × reticle radii |\n2091\t| | `exitVelocity` | 1.0 | 0.5–2.0 | × exit speed |\n2092\t| | `launchSpread` | 1.0 | 0–2 | × the launch-angle response to reticle offset |\n2093\t| Ball | `gravity` | 1.0 | 0.3–2.5 | × 520 U/s² |\n2094\t| | `drag` | 0.05 | 0–0.3 | per second |\n2095\t| | `bounce` | 1.0 | 0.3–1.5 | × surface restitution |\n2096\t| | `rollFriction` | 1.0 | 0.3–3 | × rolling deceleration |\n2097\t| | `wind` | 1.0 | 0–3 | × the park's wind |\n2098\t| Players | `runSpeed` | 1.0 | 0.5–2 | × runners |\n2099\t| | `fielderSpeed` | 1.0 | 0.5–2 | × fielders |\n2100\t| | `throwSpeed` | 1.0 | 0.5–2 | × throws |\n2101\t| | `catchRadius` | 1.0 | 0.5–2.5 | × catch reach |\n2102\t| | `turboPower` | 1.0 | 0–2 | × the turbo boost |\n2103\t| | `turboDrain` | 1.0 | 0–3 | × the drain |\n2104\t| Over the top | `meterGain` | 1.0 | 0–5 | × meter gains |\n2105\t| | `batzookaPower` | 1.6 | 1.0–3.0 | the Batzooka's exit multiplier |\n2106\t| | `rhubarbChance` | 0.4 | 0–1 | chance on a hard HBP |\n2107\t| | `hazardRate` | 1.0 | 0–4 | × hazard frequency |\n2108\t| CPU | `cpuBat` `cpuPitch` `cpuField` `cpuRun` | 1.0 | 0–2 | × CPU skill |\n2109\t| Camera | `plateDist` | 72 | 40–140 | U behind the plate |\n2110\t| | `plateHeight` | 36 | 16–90 | camera height |\n2111\t| | `plateFov` | 46 | 30–80 | degrees |\n2112\t| | `fieldZoom` | 1.0 | 0.4–2 | × Broadcast zoom |\n2113\t| | `heightSquash` | 0.45 | 0.2–1 | drawn height above 40 U |\n2114\t| Game | `gameSpeed` | 1.0 | 0.25–2 | `game.timeScale` |\n2115\t\n2116\t## Appendix B: Controls\n2117\t\n2118\tThe full action table and the per-context button meanings are in §6.14. The same tables appear in the Playbook, drawn\n2119\twith the device's glyphs.\n2120\t\n2121\t## Appendix C: Bus events\n2122\t\n2123\t`scene`, `pitchSelect`, `windup`, `release`, `pitchCross`, `swing`, `contact`, `miss`, `call` ({ kind: 'strike' |\n2124\t'ball' | 'foul' }), `walk`, `hbp`, `strikeout`, `inPlay`, `fielded`, `catch` ({ fly, dive, wall }), `drop`, `throw`,\n2125\t`throwError`, `out` ({ how: 'fly' | 'force' | 'tag' | 'k' | 'pickoff' }), `safe`, `advance`, `run`, `homer` ({ dist,\n2126\tbatzooka, target }), `groundRuleDouble`, `steal` ({ ok }), `pickoff`, `doublePlay`, `meter` ({ team, value }),\n2127\t`meterFull`, `super` ({ kind }), `turbo`, `dive`, `climb`, `slide`, `bowlOver`, `rhubarbStart`, `rhubarbEnd`, `hazard`\n2128\t({ kind }), `halfEnd`, `inningEnd`, `leadChange`, `walkoff`, `gameEnd`, `replay`, `cinematic`, `lesson` ({ id, passed\n2129\t}), `tourStop` ({ stop, won }), `purchase`, `derbyHit`, `hubState`.\n2130\t\n2131\t## Appendix D: `game.debug`\n2132\t\n2133\t| Member | What |\n2134\t|---|---|\n2135\t| `snapshot()` | `{ scene, phase, inning, half, outs, balls, strikes, score: [away, home], bases: [ids], batter, pitcher, ball: { x, y, z, vx, vy, vz, mode }, lastContact: { timingMs, dx, dz, Q, EV, launch, spray }, meters, turbo, fielders: [{ pos, x, y, state }], runners: [{ id, base, target, state }], cam: 'plate' \\| 'broadcast' \\| 'moonshot' \\| 'replay', ctx, tour: { stop, fb }, attract: { on, segment }, hub: { active, phase, score, sent }, dev: { open, tab }, touchOnly, device, glyphs, errors }` |\n2136\t| `setup(o)` | `{ park, away, home, inning, half, outs, balls, strikes, score, bases, batterIdx, meters, turbo, seed, difficulty }`: places a situation at once |\n2137\t| `force(o)` | `{ nextPitch: { type, x, z, q }, contact: 'perfect' \\| 'miss' \\| { timingMs, dx, dz, swing }, hazard: 'now', rhubarb: true, homer: true }` |\n2138\t| `tune`, `resetTune()` | the live TUNE object and the reset |\n2139\t| `events` | the bus's ring buffer |\n2140\t| `bot` | `{ on(side, { level, cheats }), off(side) }`: the bot plays that side through its inputs |\n2141\t| `step(n)`, `skip(phase)` | n fixed steps; jump past a cinematic or phase |\n2142\t| `warp(scene, data)` | the dev WARP, for tests |\n2143\t| `hubMock(info)` | installs a fake `AIHub` for headless hub tests |\n2144\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a605ca8e-6f21-4c44-bd74-b97a2b38e121","uuid":"e8130847-3ffe-4acc-911f-cb187e77bf00","timestamp":"2026-11-04T13:01:37.752Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium.build__20261104-060114__x4549c1/work/PLAN.md","content":"  planning), run Playwright and Chromium with `TMPDIR=<dev>/.tmp`.\n- Write `tools/build.mjs` (concat `src/` into `build/game.js`; bundle `../BatzookaBaseball-Baseball-claude-opus-5-5-max-20261103-174819.html` per §12).\n- Write `tests/run.mjs` and the headless loader (§11.2); `index.html`; the `00-core` spine (registries, bus, RNG,\n  TUNE); the boot, title and match scene skeletons; the `game.debug` skeleton.\n- Make engine changes 1, 2, 4 and 5 (§3.3), and a first `#gallery` scene (rigs on a plain field) to look at the bat and\n  mitt; the full gallery comes with dev mode in M5.\n- **Done when:** the bundle opens to a title in `tools/check.mjs` with no errors, the smoke test passes, and the\n  gallery shows a rig holding a bat and wearing a mitt.\n\n**M1: The at-bat** (the core, and the biggest risk; §10 R1 and R2).\n- Field geometry and the Kernel Field TileMap; the Plate Cam with the fence, stands and towers.\n- The pitcher, batter and catcher rigs with clips or fallbacks.\n- Pitch types, windup, release ring, aftertouch; the reticle, swings and contact model; the count rules and calls.\n- Batted-ball physics with home run, foul and fair detection; the Broadcast Cam showing the ball's flight.\n- Umpire stamps, basic sounds, the timing feedback and the dev timing bar.\n- For this milestone only, a ball in play resolves at its landing as a \"HIT!\" or \"OUT!\" stamp by a simple rule. M3\n  replaces this with real fielding.\n- **Done when:** T-PITCH, T-BAT, T-BALL and T-RULES (the count part) pass; 200 bot at-bats against the CPU give a\n  sensible spread (whiffs, fouls, grounders, flies, line drives and some home runs, from the contact readouts); Plate Cam\n  screenshots at 1280×720 and 1920×1080 show a readable zone, batter, pitcher and ball.\n\n**M2: The Derby and the AI Hub** (early, to settle the protocol and the bundle; §10 R7 and R8).\n- The Derby: local play with 1–4 players hot seat, targets, scoring, the initials table.\n- `40-hub.js`: connect, our card, ready, start, progress, result, time-up, end, ghosts.\n- The session rules, the meta tags, and the session client placement in the bundle.\n- **Done when:** T-DERBY and T-HUB pass headless, and `window.__hubCheck.pass` is true in the real harness for\n  `players=2&auto=1`, `players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1` and `&scenario=host-leave`; the bundle still opens normally outside\n  a hub.\n\n**M3: Fielding, running and the full game.**\n- Fielders (assignment, chase, catch, throw, cutoffs, tags, forces, rundowns); baserunners (forces, tag-ups, orders,\n  steals, pickoffs, slides).\n- The full rules engine (innings, end of game, extra innings, mercy, errors).\n- The human fielding and running controls, mouse included; the CPU brains; line scores and the results screen.\n- **Done when:** T-RULES, T-FIELD, T-RUN and T-AI pass (CPU vs CPU sims in range), and a 3-inning game with the bot\n  as player 1 (through the real controls) against the CPU plays from start to finish with no stuck play.\n\n**M4: The over-the-top layer.**\n- The meter and all supers; turbo; dive, jump and wall climb; headfirst dives; the bowl-over.\n- The Moonshot Cam, fireworks and the trot; replays; the crowd, hype and the wave; the jumbotron; mascots;\n  between-innings shows; the Rhubarb.\n- The commentary director with the babble voices; all music and sound effects.\n- **Done when:** T-SUPER, T-RHU, T-CAM, T-TALK, T-AUD and T-CROWD pass, and filmstrips of the swing, pitch, dive,\n  slide, wall climb, umpire calls and Rhubarb punches look clean (wind-up, strike, settle).\n\n**M5: The front end, input polish, dev mode and saves.**\n- Title (with its mode menu), Team Select with joining (1–4), results, Playbook, the pause items, About/Credits (with\n  provisional feedback text, rewritten in M8).\n- Our settings; the glyph renderer and prompts (PlayStation by default, Xbox by setting, keyboard, mouse); mouse\n  hover and clicks on every screen and in the world.\n- The touch-only card; dev mode (all six tabs, pinned sliders, the gallery); saves.\n- **Done when:** T-UI, T-IN, T-HUD, T-DEV, T-MP and T-TOUCH pass, and screenshots of the prompts for a PlayStation pad,\n  an Xbox setting, the keyboard and the mouse look right.\n\n**M6: Content.**\n- All six teams and rosters with the captains' signatures and team supers; the six parks with their looks, lights and\n  hazards; the boss rules.\n- The Tour (map, clubhouse, rewards, every cutscene, the ending and credits roll); Spring Training's eight lessons.\n- All line pools.\n- **Done when:** T-HAZ, T-TOUR and T-TRAIN pass, the playthrough test passes, and screenshots of every park in both\n  main cameras look like their descriptions.\n\n**M7: The attract mode.**\n- The director and the ten segments, the idle detection, exiting on input, touch-only compatibility.\n- **Done when:** T-ATT passes and a filmed loop (screenshots every 10 s across one loop) shows every segment.\n\n**M8: Polish, verify and ship.**\n- **Balance:** sims and slider sessions; then write the tuned defaults into `TUNE` (the \"reset to defaults\" values).\n- **Look:** act on every `check.mjs` look note; check every park and screen at TV size.\n- **Animation:** a filmstrip pass.\n- **Writing:** a pass over every line for tone, length and repetition.\n- **Feedback:** write the final About text and the four feedback sections.\n- **Ship:** grep for leftovers (§12); `exit-interview.json`; the final bundle; every test, the browser checks and the\n  hub harness green.\n\n---\n\n## 10. Risks and how to take them down\n\n| # | Risk | Why it is risky | De-risk early | Fallback |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| R1 | The Plate Cam (Mode 7) doesn't read: the batter hides the zone, near rigs look odd, walls sort wrong | Mode 7's billboards are mostly used for karts, not near-camera people | Prototype on day one of M1, with screenshots at both box sides; every camera number in TUNE; the batter offset to the side, the camera shifted 4 U the other way; the catcher at 85% opacity | A custom low `E.View` (pitch 18) from behind the plate, with the ball's size scaled by its distance and drawn by hand (an orthographic view) |\n| R2 | Batting isn't fun or fair | Timing, aim and outcome must feel causal | A deterministic pitch path with a known crossing; the dev timing bar and contact readout; timing feedback text; unit tests of the contact mapping; sims of outcome rates; assists by difficulty | Widen the windows and sweet spot by TUNE; an aim assist that pulls the reticle 30% toward the ball |\n| R3 | Rules edge cases (forces, tag-ups, third-out timing) | Baseball's rules are subtle | A pure rules module with a table-driven test of 24+ situations; explicit lists of kept and dropped rules | Simplify the case (for example, auto-return runners on caught flies) and say so in House Rules |\n| R4 | Fielding AI looks dumb: two fielders on one ball, nobody covering | Roles depend on the situation | A role table by ball direction and runners; a test of coverage in each situation; one chaser at a time | Auto-assign the cover men by the nearest open base |\n| R5 | Fly balls leave the screen in the Broadcast Cam | High apexes | The display height squash, the landing marker, `cam.frame` zooming out to 0.5 | A small picture-in-picture \"ball cam\" in a corner showing the ball against the sky |\n| R6 | Mocap clips fit badly (the bat's direction, long takes, mirroring) | CMU takes are raw | The window finder; review in the gallery with filmstrips; procedural fallbacks already written | Use the procedural moves for that motion |\n| R7 | The hub protocol fails in the single file | Ordering of scripts, the card, cadence | Build it in M2, run the real harness then and keep it in `--hub`; the mock in headless tests; follow §6.21 to the letter | Parallel mode (drop the ghost traffic and change one meta), if ghosts are the failing check |\n| R8 | The bundle breaks: `</script>` inside inlined code, an external request, the file:// origin | Inlining 1.3 MB of code | The build scans for `</script` and `<!--` in the inlined code and fails if it finds them; `check.mjs` lists external requests (there must be none); test both file:// and served | Split the inlined code into several `<script>` blocks |\n| R9 | PlayStation symbols missing from the font | The 5×7 font is ASCII plus a few symbols | The icon renderer, plus the four glyphs added to the font; T-HUD checks every label | – |\n| R10 | Scope: many systems and much content | A demo with a whole Tour | Strict milestones; content as data; the playthrough test catches regressions | Quick Tour games (1 inning) by default if time runs short (the setting exists anyway) |\n| R11 | The attract director is brittle with forced outcomes | Scripted events can miss | A time limit per segment and moving on by itself; forced outcomes through `game.debug.force` | Skip the segment and log it (a test fails if any segment is skipped) |\n| R12 | Determinism drifts (tests flake) | Cosmetic code using `Math.random` in the rules | The rng-stream rule; the proof hash twice per run (T-CORE) | – |\n| R13 | The shared machine: a full `/tmp`, ports, other agents | Seen while planning | `TMPDIR` in the dev folder; the server on 127.0.0.1 with port 0; stop only your own PIDs | – |\n\n---\n\n## 11. Testing\n\n### 11.1 One command\n\n`node tests/run.mjs` (also `npm test`) runs every headless suite and prints **only failures**, then one line:\n`212 passed, 0 failed (38.4 s)`. The exit code is 1 on any failure.\n- `--browser` adds the browser checks (§11.6), `--hub` the AI Hub harness (§11.7), `--full` the long balance sims\n  (§11.5); `--all` runs everything.\n- `--only <suite>` reruns one suite. Rerun a suite only after changing the code it covers.\n- Tests and tools play the game headless and read its state. Screenshots are only for what a script can't judge: the\n  look, framing and readability.\n- Per TASK.md, no subagents or workflows debate, review, judge or audit.\n\n**The shared machine:**\n- Prefer file:// and the headless tools.\n- The hub harness needs a server: `tools/serve.mjs` binds **127.0.0.1 on port 0** and prints the port the OS picked (or\n  `python3 -m http.server 0 --bind 127.0.0.1`). Fetch the page once to confirm it is this game (its `<title>` is\n  \"Batzooka Baseball\") before trusting a result.\n- Stop only the processes you started, by their PID. Never use `pkill`, `killall`, `fuser -k`, or kill whatever holds\n  a port.\n- Don't read files outside the dev folder and this folder, apart from the sources in §3.1.\n- If `/tmp` is full, set `TMPDIR=<dev>/.tmp` for Playwright.\n\n### 11.2 The headless harness and `game.debug`\n\n`tests/lib/load.mjs` makes a `vm` context with the stand-ins the kits' test uses (`window`, `addEventListener`,\n`location`), plus `navigator`, `matchMedia` and a fake `AIHub` when asked. It runs `engine/my-3d2dge.js`, the mocap\nfiles and `build/game.js` in it, and returns `{ E, game, BZ }`.\n- Tests drive the game with `game.advance(seconds)` (exact 1/120 s steps), `game.input.tap / hold`, `addPlayer` and\n  `input.feed` (mouse), and read `game.debug.snapshot()`.\n- The bots (§6.11) play real controls.\n- A determinism check (T-CORE-03) runs the same seeded half-inning twice and compares the hash of its snapshots, then\n  once more with `Math.random` seeded differently, where the gameplay hash must not change.\n\n`game.debug` (Appendix D) has `snapshot`, `setup`, `force`, `tune`, `resetTune`, `events`, `bot`, `step`, `skip`,\n`warp` and `hubMock`.\n\n### 11.3 The test catalog\n\n| Suite | IDs | Covers |\n|---|---|---|\n| core | T-CORE-01..05 | registries; the bus; RNG streams; determinism (the same seeded half-inning twice gives the same snapshot hash, and a third run with `Math.random` seeded differently gives the same gameplay hash of score, outs, bases and ball path, which proves the rules never use `Math.random`); TUNE meta complete (every key has a label, range and default) |\n| rules | T-RULES-01..24 | §6.1 |\n| pitch | T-PITCH-01..12 | §6.2 |\n| bat | T-BAT-01..14 | §6.3 |\n| ball | T-BALL-01..12 | §6.4 |\n| field | T-FIELD-01..16 | §6.5 |\n| run | T-RUN-01..14 | §6.6 |\n| super | T-SUPER-01..10 | §6.7 |\n| rhubarb | T-RHU-01..06 | §6.9 |\n| hazards | T-HAZ-01..08 | §6.10 |\n| ai | T-AI-01..08 | §6.11 (sims in §11.5) |\n| cams | T-CAM-01..07 | §6.12 |\n| hud | T-HUD-01..08 | §6.13 |\n| input | T-IN-01..10 | §6.14 |\n| talk | T-TALK-01..07 | §6.15 |\n| audio | T-AUD-01..04 | §6.16 |\n| crowd | T-CROWD-01..04 | §6.17 |\n| modes | T-TOUR-01..06, T-TRAIN-01..08, T-DERBY-01..06 | Tour progression, rewards, clubhouse purchases change stats, save and load round-trip; each lesson's pass condition is reachable by its lesson bot; Derby outs, scoring, Golden Balls, targets, the initials table |\n| mp | T-MP-01..05 | §6.20 |\n| hub | T-HUB-01..08 | §6.21, with the mock |\n| attract | T-ATT-01..05 | §6.22 |\n| dev | T-DEV-01..06 | §6.23 |\n| ui | T-UI-01..06 | §6.24 |\n| touch | T-TOUCH-01..03 | §6.26 |\n| about | T-ABOUT-01..03 | every Source Information field present and non-empty; the four feedback sections present; the version label shows |\n| playthrough | T-PLAY-01 | §11.4 |\n\n### 11.4 The scripted playthrough of the whole game (T-PLAY-01)\n\nOne test, run by the bot through the real inputs with `BZ.cosmetic = false`, with no errors allowed anywhere\n(`game.errors` empty at every step) and a real-time limit (measure the run once, then fix the limit at about 1.5× that,\nand at most 5 minutes):\n1. Boot to the title. Idle 10.5 s: the attract mode starts. Let its whole reel loop once. A tap returns to the title.\n2. **Spring Training:** all eight lessons, by their lesson bots, each reaching \"LESSON PASSED!\".\n3. **New Tour in slot 1, with Tour game length Quick:**\n   - Prologue: advance with ✕.\n   - Each of the five stops: its pregame, its game, its postgame. In the games the player-1 bot plays at the \"Batzooka\"\n     level against a Rookie CPU, with the dev cheat \"perfect contact\" on for the bot's side only, so every stop is\n     won in bounded time.\n   - After each stop: buy one upgrade in the clubhouse; save.\n   - Check the scripted Rhubarb at Caldera, the Rally Cap or the boss's short circuit at the MegaDome, the ending and\n     the credits roll, and the return to the title.\n4. **Load slot 1** and confirm the Tour is complete and everything is unlocked.\n5. **Exhibition with four bot players** (two a side) for one inning in a random park; the results screen.\n6. **Derby** with two hot-seat bots; the initials entry.\n7. **Hub round** with the mock: card, ready, start, progress, result, end.\n8. Open the About screen and every page; open the pause menu, then Dev Mode, move a slider, reset it.\n\n### 11.5 Balance sims (part of the `ai` suite)\n\n- Seeded CPU-vs-CPU 9-inning games at Pro must land in the ranges of T-AI-01: 6 games in the default run, 30 with\n  `--full` (`M.fast = true` keeps them quick).\n- Each difficulty pairing: in the default run, the higher level must score more runs in total over 3 seeded games;\n  with `--full`, it must win at least 60% of 10.\n- A bot batter against each pitch type: the contact rate is 55–85% at Pro.\n- The Batzooka's home run rate on contact is 70–95%.\n- The mean Derby round score of the bot is 1,500–4,000 ft.\n\nThese sims only report. The defaults are tuned with them and the sliders in M8, and the ranges stay as tests.\n\n### 11.6 Browser checks (`--browser`)\n\n- `node tools/check.mjs <bundle>.html` at the default 1280×720, then with `#match`, `#derby`, `#about`, `#gallery`,\n  then `--size 1920x1080`, and `#touch --size 390x844@3` (the touch-only card). There must be no errors, no external\n  requests (the bundle is offline), and the canvas covered. Act on every look note.\n- `tools/filmstrip.mjs` strips (with `--seed 1`, so they repeat) of the swing (contact, power, Batzooka), the pitch,\n  the throw, the dive, the slide, the wall climb, the umpire calls and the Rhubarb punches. Look at each: wind-up,\n  strike and settle, with no jerks or backward sweeps.\n- **Screenshots only for what scripts can't judge.** Look at each:\n  - the Plate Cam in each park and both batter's boxes;\n  - the Broadcast Cam on a deep fly;\n  - the HUD at 1920×1080 (a TV);\n  - prompts for the pad (PlayStation and Xbox), the keyboard and the mouse;\n  - the title, Team Select, the Tour Map, the clubhouse, the results, Dev Mode, the About pages;\n  - the Moonshot Cam;\n  - each hazard;\n  - the touch-only card.\n\n### 11.7 The AI Hub harness (`--hub`)\n\n`tests/hub.mjs` (Playwright):\n1. Copy the bundle beside `hub/harness.html`, `bridge.js` and `round.js`, and start `tools/serve.mjs` (127.0.0.1,\n   port 0).\n2. Open `harness.html?game=<bundle>.html&players=2&auto=1`. Wait for `document.body.dataset.complete === 'true'`, then\n   require `window.__hubCheck.pass === true`, and print the failing checks if not.\n3. Repeat with `players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1`, and with `players=2&scenario=host-leave&auto=1`.\n4. Open the bundle alone to confirm it reaches the title outside a session.\n5. Stop the server by its PID.\n\n---\n\n## 12. Packaging and hand-off\n\n**`tools/build.mjs` writes the single file** `BatzookaBaseball-Baseball-claude-opus-5-5-max-20261103-174819.html`\ninto this folder (the dev folder's parent), from this template:\n```html\n<!doctype html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n<meta charset=\"utf-8\">\n<script>/* vendor/aihub-session.js, unmodified, inlined: the first script, right after meta charset */</script>\n<meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1, viewport-fit=cover\">\n<title>Batzooka Baseball</title>\n<meta name=\"description\" content=\"Over-the-top arcade baseball: fireball pitches, a rocket-powered bat, wall-climbing catches and bench-clearing rhubarbs.\">\n<!-- the hub tags of §6.21 -->\n<style>html,body{margin:0;height:100%;background:#000;overflow:hidden}#screen{width:100%;height:100%;display:block;image-rendering:pixelated;touch-action:none}</style>\n</head>\n<body>\n<!-- E.bootSplash('BATZOOKA BASEBALL') markup, as the handoff's index.html has it -->\n<canvas id=\"screen\"></canvas>\n<script>/* engine/my-3d2dge.js */</script>\n<script>/* engine/mocap-readable.js + engine/mocap.js + assets/mocap-batzooka.js */</script>\n<script>/* build/game.js */</script>\n</body>\n</html>\n```\n\n**Build rules:**\n- **Inlined code:** inline each file as is. If one contains `</script` or `<!--`, stop with an error naming the file\n  and line, and fix the source (don't escape blindly).\n- **No outside requests:** no CDN and no network; the page works from file://.\n- **Size:** the bundle is about 1.5–2 MB, which is fine.\n- **The hub client:** after building, check that the bundle's first `<script>` is the hub client, byte-identical to\n  `vendor/aihub-session.js`.\n\n**Before handing back:**\n1. Every test is green with `node tests/run.mjs --all`, including the playthrough, the browser checks and the hub\n   harness.\n2. No leftovers: `grep -rniE \"TODO|FIXME|XXX|placeholder|lorem|stub|not implemented\" src/` finds nothing, and no\n   screen, line or button says \"coming soon\".\n3. The About/Credits screen shows the final Source Information and the three feedback sections, answered honestly (the\n   number of issues testing caught, how many were critical, the most and least helpful tests; the six engine answers;\n   the four prompt answers), with \"unknown\" where something can't be confirmed.\n4. **`exit-interview.json`** sits in this folder beside the .html, in exactly TASK.md's shape, with every value filled\n   in (§6.27 for `aiHub`). It must parse:\n   `node -e \"JSON.parse(require('fs').readFileSync('exit-interview.json','utf8'))\"`.\n5. `ENGINE-CHANGES.md` is complete, and the same list is in the engine feedback.\n6. **The final chat reply** holds the Source Information, the Testing Feedback, the Engine Feedback and the Prompt\n   Feedback (as TASK.md requires), and a short summary of the game.\n\n---\n\n## Appendix A: `BZ.TUNE` defaults (the dev sliders)\n\n| Group | Key | Default | Min–max | Meaning |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Pitching | `pitchSpeed` | 1.0 | 0.5–2.0 | × every pitch's speed |\n| | `pitchBreak` | 1.0 | 0–2.5 | × break |\n| | `aftertouch` | 1.0 | 0–3 | × in-flight steering |\n| | `releaseWindow` | 1.0 | 0.3–3 | × the perfect-release window |\n| | `staminaDrain` | 1.0 | 0–3 | × stamina cost |\n| Batting | `swingTiming` | 1.0 | 0.3–3 | × the timing windows |\n| | `sweetSpot` | 1.0 | 0.4–2.5 | × reticle radii |\n| | `exitVelocity` | 1.0 | 0.5–2.0 | × exit speed |\n| | `launchSpread` | 1.0 | 0–2 | × the launch-angle response to reticle offset |\n| Ball | `gravity` | 1.0 | 0.3–2.5 | × 520 U/s² |\n| | `drag` | 0.05 | 0–0.3 | per second |\n| | `bounce` | 1.0 | 0.3–1.5 | × surface restitution |\n| | `rollFriction` | 1.0 | 0.3–3 | × rolling deceleration |\n| | `wind` | 1.0 | 0–3 | × the park's wind |\n| Players | `runSpeed` | 1.0 | 0.5–2 | × runners |\n| | `fielderSpeed` | 1.0 | 0.5–2 | × fielders |\n| | `throwSpeed` | 1.0 | 0.5–2 | × throws |\n| | `catchRadius` | 1.0 | 0.5–2.5 | × catch reach |\n| | `turboPower` | 1.0 | 0–2 | × the turbo boost |\n| | `turboDrain` | 1.0 | 0–3 | × the drain |\n| Over the top | `meterGain` | 1.0 | 0–5 | × meter gains |\n| | `batzookaPower` | 1.6 | 1.0–3.0 | the Batzooka's exit multiplier |\n| | `rhubarbChance` | 0.4 | 0–1 | chance on a hard HBP |\n| | `hazardRate` | 1.0 | 0–4 | × hazard frequency |\n| CPU | `cpuBat` `cpuPitch` `cpuField` `cpuRun` | 1.0 | 0–2 | × CPU skill |\n| Camera | `plateDist` | 72 | 40–140 | U behind the plate |\n| | `plateHeight` | 36 | 16–90 | camera height |\n| | `plateFov` | 46 | 30–80 | degrees |\n| | `fieldZoom` | 1.0 | 0.4–2 | × Broadcast zoom |\n| | `heightSquash` | 0.45 | 0.2–1 | drawn height above 40 U |\n| Game | `gameSpeed` | 1.0 | 0.25–2 | `game.timeScale` |\n\n## Appendix B: Controls\n\nThe full action table and the per-context button meanings are in §6.14. The same tables appear in the Playbook, drawn\nwith the device's glyphs.\n\n## Appendix C: Bus events\n\n`scene`, `pitchSelect`, `windup`, `release`, `pitchCross`, `swing`, `contact`, `miss`, `call` ({ kind: 'strike' |\n'ball' | 'foul' }), `walk`, `hbp`, `strikeout`, `inPlay`, `fielded`, `catch` ({ fly, dive, wall }), `drop`, `throw`,\n`throwError`, `out` ({ how: 'fly' | 'force' | 'tag' | 'k' | 'pickoff' }), `safe`, `advance`, `run`, `homer` ({ dist,\nbatzooka, target }), `groundRuleDouble`, `steal` ({ ok }), `pickoff`, `doublePlay`, `meter` ({ team, value }),\n`meterFull`, `super` ({ kind }), `turbo`, `dive`, `climb`, `slide`, `bowlOver`, `rhubarbStart`, `rhubarbEnd`, `hazard`\n({ kind }), `halfEnd`, `inningEnd`, `leadChange`, `walkoff`, `gameEnd`, `replay`, `cinematic`, `lesson` ({ id, passed\n}), `tourStop` ({ stop, won }), `purchase`, `derbyHit`, `hubState`.\n\n## Appendix D: `game.debug`\n\n| Member | What |\n|---|---|\n| `snapshot()` | `{ scene, phase, inning, half, outs, balls, strikes, score: [away, home], bases: [ids], batter, pitcher, ball: { x, y, z, vx, vy, vz, mode }, lastContact: { timingMs, dx, dz, Q, EV, launch, spray }, meters, turbo, fielders: [{ pos, x, y, state }], runners: [{ id, base, target, state }], cam: 'plate' \\| 'broadcast' \\| 'moonshot' \\| 'replay', ctx, tour: { stop, fb }, attract: { on, segment }, hub: { active, phase, score, sent }, dev: { open, tab }, touchOnly, device, glyphs, errors }` |\n| `setup(o)` | `{ park, away, home, inning, half, outs, balls, strikes, score, bases, batterIdx, meters, turbo, seed, difficulty }`: places a situation at once |\n| `force(o)` | `{ nextPitch: { type, x, z, q }, contact: 'perfect' \\| 'miss' \\| { timingMs, dx, dz, swing }, hazard: 'now', rhubarb: true, homer: true }` |\n| `tune`, `resetTune()` | the live TUNE object and the reset |\n| `events` | the bus's ring buffer |\n| `bot` | `{ on(side, { level, cheats }), off(side) }`: the bot plays that side through its inputs |\n| `step(n)`, `skip(phase)` | n fixed steps; jump past a cinematic or phase |\n| `warp(scene, data)` | the dev WARP, for tests |\n| `hubMock(info)` | installs a fake `AIHub` for headless hub tests |\n","numLines":345,"startLine":1800,"totalLines":2144}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_019Wd6cPcNg85NKof9kdPNpJ","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
