{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgi2PcKznTWX3SjGUG8P9","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01LuzoD2jzmwC97Pw1M7iAxi","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"sed -i \"s/const W = r.W, H = r.H, mx = 30, my = 40, mw = W - 60, mh = H - 112;/const W = r.W, H = r.H, mx = 30, my = 40, mw = W - 60, mh = H - 122;/; s/text(g, TOUR.map.cur.sub, W \\/ 2, my + mh + 2, '#ffe680', { align: 'center' });/text(g, TOUR.map.cur.sub, W \\/ 2, my + mh + 4, '#ffe680', { align: 'center' });/\" src/33-tour.js; date '+%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S'; cat > ENGINE-CHANGES.md <<'EOF'\n# Engine changes (my-3D2dge v0.85.2 handoff copy, engine/my-3d2dge.js)\n\nEvery change is small and marked `BATZOOKA` in the source.\n\n1. **`weapon: 'bat'` on `E.Humanoid`.** Added to the built-in weapon list (it used to warn and draw a sword), with a rest\n   direction (the bat up over the back shoulder), a `tip()` length of 12, and a draw branch in both the HD and the\n   classic styles: a tapered capsule (knob, thin handle, thick barrel) in `colors.bat`. Why: a baseball game needs a bat\n   that swings with the engine's own attack specs.\n2. **`mitt` option on `E.Humanoid`** (`'left'` or `'right'`, with `mittSize`): a leather mitt drawn over the glove hand\n   in `colors.mitt`. Why: fielders and catchers read as baseball players at a glance.\n3. **Font glyphs** `✕ ○ □ △ · ✓ ■ ● —` added to the 5×7 font. Why: `input.label()` returns PlayStation symbols and the\n   UI uses a few marks the font lacked (they drew as `?`).\n4. **The `glyphs` setting** (Controller, \"Button symbols\") now defaults to PlayStation and offers PlayStation or Xbox;\n   `input.glyphs` starts as `'playstation'`. Why: TASK.md asks for PlayStation glyphs on any pad by default, with a\n   Settings option for Xbox.\n5. **Fixed my own first edit:** a `//` comment appended mid-line in the settings table swallowed the rest of the line\n   (a syntax error); it is a `/* */` comment now. Caught by the first headless load.\nEOF\necho ok","description":"Tour map nudge; write ENGINE-CHANGES.md; get time"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4110,"cache_read_input_tokens":620187,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4110},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a605ca8e-6f21-4c44-bd74-b97a2b38e121","uuid":"d4a4f171-432a-4f0f-b7c0-8074b145dbd5","timestamp":"2026-11-04T14:12:39.162Z","request_id":"req_011Cgi2PbwgZnHvqjT5sYg4K","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01LuzoD2jzmwC97Pw1M7iAxi":{"command":"sed -i \"s/const W = r.W, H = r.H, mx = 30, my = 40, mw = W - 60, mh = H - 112;/const W = r.W, H = r.H, mx = 30, my = 40, mw = W - 60, mh = H - 122;/; s/text(g, TOUR.map.cur.sub, W \\/ 2, my + mh + 2, '#ffe680', { align: 'center' });/text(g, TOUR.map.cur.sub, W \\/ 2, my + mh + 4, '#ffe680', { align: 'center' });/\" src/33-tour.js; date '+%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S'; cat > ENGINE-CHANGES.md <<'EOF'\n# Engine changes (my-3D2dge v0.85.2 handoff copy, engine/my-3d2dge.js)\n\nEvery change is small and marked `BATZOOKA` in the source.\n\n1. **`weapon: 'bat'` on `E.Humanoid`.** Added to the built-in weapon list (it used to warn and draw a sword), with a rest\n   direction (the bat up over the back shoulder), a `tip()` length of 12, and a draw branch in both the HD and the\n   classic styles: a tapered capsule (knob, thin handle, thick barrel) in `colors.bat`. Why: a baseball game needs a bat\n   that swings with the engine's own attack specs.\n2. **`mitt` option on `E.Humanoid`** (`'left'` or `'right'`, with `mittSize`): a leather mitt drawn over the glove hand\n   in `colors.mitt`. Why: fielders and catchers read as baseball players at a glance.\n3. **Font glyphs** `✕ ○ □ △ · ✓ ■ ● —` added to the 5×7 font. Why: `input.label()` returns PlayStation symbols and the\n   UI uses a few marks the font lacked (they drew as `?`).\n4. **The `glyphs` setting** (Controller, \"Button symbols\") now defaults to PlayStation and offers PlayStation or Xbox;\n   `input.glyphs` starts as `'playstation'`. Why: TASK.md asks for PlayStation glyphs on any pad by default, with a\n   Settings option for Xbox.\n5. **Fixed my own first edit:** a `//` comment appended mid-line in the settings table swallowed the rest of the line\n   (a syntax error); it is a `/* */` comment now. Caught by the first headless load.\nEOF\necho ok","description":"Tour map nudge; write ENGINE-CHANGES.md; get time"}}}
