{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgi3EJeytNjntUvQ3U2Cy","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Everything checks out. All three deliverables are in `work/`, the folder that holds STAGE.md and TASK.md, so that is \"this folder's root\". The last full run passed 106 of 106 checks, and every TASK.md feature has an automated check or a hand-run check listed below.\n\n**What's in the folder**\n- `BatzookaBaseball-Baseball-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261104-060114.html`: the game. It is the exact name TASK.md asks for, and it sits next to the dev folder of the same name.\n- `exit-interview.json`: parses, and no field is empty.\n- **TODO/placeholder/stub search:** 0 hits in the game code. The bundle as a whole has 4 hits, all inside the engine's own code (one is an internal helper called `_pStub`); none is an unfinished feature.\n\n**Each TASK.md feature and what checks it**\n\n| TASK.md feature | Checked by |\n|---|---|\n| Genre and perspective: arcade baseball; pseudo-3D view behind the catcher, three-quarter field view, home-run chase camera | screenshots of all six parks |\n| Title chosen by a random number generator | the plan's draw (37 = *Batzooka Baseball*) |\n| Single HTML file, from a dev subfolder | built bundle; AI Hub client is the first script, unchanged; no external requests |\n| Built on the my-3D2dge engine | `ENGINE-CHANGES.md` lists the five changes |\n| Art | the engine's pixel art, plus code-drawn parks, props, crowds and mascots |\n| Animation | the engine's own rig system, plus new swing, bunt, pitch, umpire and brawl motions; animation gallery scene |\n| Audio, all in code | 14 songs, 7 stings, 45 effects, gibberish babble voices for 16 characters |\n| Online: AI Hub | real harness passed: 2 players; 4 players with latency, jitter and loss; host leaves |\n| Online: protocol details | headless tests: ready with no key press, no `Math.random` on the card, progress every second, one result, time-up, behaviour after the round ends |\n| Local multiplayer | four-player exhibition plays to the end; second player joins on half the keyboard; duties split between two players on a side |\n| Complete demo of every mode | scripted bot playthrough: Tour prologue, all 5 stops including the boss, the scripted brawl, ending, credits, unlocks; all 8 lessons; hot-seat Derby with initials; pickoff and replay checks |\n| Dev mode from the pause menu | pause menu has it; sliders change live; reset to defaults; cheats; situation editor; warps |\n| Attract mode | starts after 10 s idle on the title or a top menu; all 10 segments run and loop; any input returns; never starts during play |\n| Narrative tone | radio-style commentary pools (6+ lines each, length-checked) and cutscene scripts |\n| Controller-first UI | PlayStation glyphs by default, Xbox setting; keyboard and mouse prompts follow the last device; mouse aims the bat and pitch, picks pitches with the wheel, clicks bases and menu items |\n| Touch-only devices | \"Controller or keyboard required\" card with a Settings button; attract mode still runs |\n| About/Credits screen and the four answer sections | on screen and in `exit-interview.json`; field-completeness test |\n| Testing | `node tests/run.mjs` prints only failures and a one-line count |\n\n\"Unknown\" appears only for cost and token usage, because no usage meter was available. TASK.md asks for \"unknown\" in exactly that case. The game doesn't use motion-capture clips; that was a PLAN.md suggestion, and TASK.md asks for the engine's own animation system, which the game uses.\n\n## Source Information\n- **Date:** 2026-11-04 06:01:14\n- **Source:** Baseball (the sport), over-the-top arcade style\n- **Plan:** PLAN.md\n- **Genre and Perspective:**\n  - Genre: arcade baseball, with a slapstick brawl mini-game (the Rhubarb) and a story Tour with upgrades.\n  - Perspective: pseudo-3D (Mode 7) view from behind the catcher for every pitch and swing; three-quarter field view, with High and Isometric options; home-run chase camera; half-speed replays.\n- **Tech:**\n  - my-3D2dge v0.85.2 (full engine with its Mode 7 module, five small changes).\n  - Plain JavaScript built from 28 source files.\n  - AI Hub Session client 1.4.0, unmodified.\n  - One self-contained HTML file.\n  - Node 24 and Playwright 1.63.0 for testing.\n- **Art Direction:** the engine's own pixel-art look, with parks, props, crowds and mascots drawn in code.\n- **Animation:** the engine's procedural rig system, plus new baseball and brawl motions.\n- **Audio:** chip synth only: 14 songs, 7 stings, 45 effects and babble voices for 16 characters.\n- **Online:** AI Hub Session Protocol v1, ghost mode, an online Derby round for 1–4 players.\n- **Testing:**\n  - Headless suite: 106 checks, including a bot playthrough.\n  - CPU-vs-CPU balance simulations.\n  - The engine's `check.mjs` browser check.\n  - Screenshots for the look.\n  - The real AI Hub harness, three scenarios.\n- **Research:** the engine's API docs and asset guide, its sports and kart example games, the Mode 7 module header, and the AI Hub README.\n- **Environment:** Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux; browser unknown\n- **Model:** Anthropic, claude-opus-5-5, reasoning effort medium\n- **Usage:** cost and tokens unknown; about 1.5 hours of session time.\n\n## Testing Feedback\n1. **How many issues did testing catch?** About 28: 12 code bugs, one balance overhaul, and about 15 layout problems.\n2. **How many would be considered critical / game breaking?** 6:\n   - two syntax errors that stopped the game loading;\n   - two NaN pitch speeds that froze the game mid-pitch;\n   - a crash when the ball was hit with no fielders set;\n   - late swings being called strikes before they could connect.\n3. **What was the most helpful test you ran?** The seeded CPU-vs-CPU simulations: they found both freezes and the stuck bunt flag, and gave the numbers I balanced the game with.\n4. **What was the least helpful test you ran?** The `check.mjs` sweep: it found nothing new.\n\n## Engine Feedback\n1. **What did you like most about the engine?** The Mode 7 module, and headless fixed-step testing with simulated button presses.\n2. **Did you get stuck or guess wrong?** Settings must be an array when the game is created. The dialog box couldn't be sized or placed to fit the HUD, so I wrote my own commentary box. A comment I added inside an engine line broke the build.\n3. **What was the most important thing you had to build yourself?** The baseball itself:\n   - pitch flight and the bat-to-ball contact model;\n   - ball physics;\n   - fielding and baserunning;\n   - the rules engine, pickoffs and replays.\n4. **What was the hardest part about using the engine?** Drawing the fence, foul walls and stands in Mode 7. It has a floor and flat billboards but no walls, so each wall section had to be projected by hand.\n5. **What did you change in the engine, and why?**\n   - Added a `'bat'` weapon so batters can swing a bat.\n   - Added a `mitt` option so fielders read as baseball players.\n   - Added the PlayStation symbols and a few UI marks to the pixel font, because they drew as \"?\".\n   - Made PlayStation the default button-symbol setting, with an Xbox option, as TASK.md asks.\n   - Fixed the comment I broke myself.\n6. **If you could change one thing about the engine, what would it be?** A Mode 7 wall primitive that projects and depth-sorts world-space polygons.\n\n## Prompt Feedback\n1. **What did you like most about this prompt?** The requirements are concrete and checkable, with a real harness for the online part.\n2. **What was confusing?** PLAN.md's file names disagree with TASK.md's, and it wasn't clear how much of the plan's scope was required.\n3. **What was the hardest thing to do?** Building every mode fully, and testing all of it, in one session.\n4. **What would you change in this prompt?** Mark which plan items are required and which are optional, and keep the plan's file names in line with TASK.md's."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":367,"cache_read_input_tokens":656663,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":367},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a605ca8e-6f21-4c44-bd74-b97a2b38e121","uuid":"be59a72f-6b00-4938-9928-5e0dac49f4de","timestamp":"2026-11-04T14:23:54.666Z","request_id":"req_011Cgi3EJ7jTV7uK2XNFHdkA"}
