{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgi3b6fk829N3V4USmw9K","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The remaining objections are already covered by output shown earlier in this session, and TASK.md's own text settles the last two. There is no open gap: no TODOs, placeholders or stubs; all 106 checks passed in the verbose run; and both deliverables are in `work/`, the folder that holds STAGE.md.\n\n- **Animation:** TASK.md line 17 says \"Use the engine's native animation system as the base. Make new animations…\". The game does exactly that: the engine's rig system, plus new motions for the swing, bunt, pitch, throw, umpire calls, brawl moves and mascots.\n- **\"Unknown\" fields:** TASK.md line 59 says to write \"unknown\" for anything I can't confirm. Line 73 asks for usage figures only if estimates are available. No usage meter was available, so cost and tokens are \"unknown\". Session time is still given.\n- **Every rival team, the scripted Rhubarb and the ending:** the verbose run printed \"stop 1\" through \"stop 5 plays to the results\", \"the scripted Rhubarb at Caldera Field\", \"the Tour ends: credits, everything unlocked\" and \"credits return to the title\". The separate per-park run showed a full match in all six parks against all six teams, each reaching the results screen with 0 errors.\n- **Playbook:** there was never a gap here. It printed \"PASS Playbook opens from the pause menu and turns pages\".\n- **Other TASK.md items** (one PASS line each in the verbose run, unless noted):\n  - Dev mode: opens, a slider moves a value, reset to defaults works.\n  - Attract mode: starts after 10 s idle, any input returns to the title.\n  - Multiplayer: local 2–4 players, plus the AI Hub protocol checks; the real harness also passed earlier in this session.\n  - Controls: PlayStation glyphs by default, an Xbox option, keyboard and mouse prompts.\n  - Touch-only devices: the card shows, and attract mode still runs.\n  - The About page and every Source Information field.\n\n## Source Information\n- **Date:** 2026-11-04 06:01:14\n- **Source:** Baseball (the sport), over-the-top arcade style\n- **Plan:** PLAN.md\n- **Genre and Perspective:** arcade baseball, plus a slapstick brawl mini-game and a story Tour. A Mode 7 view from behind the catcher for pitching and batting, a three-quarter view for play in the field, and a chase camera for home runs.\n- **Tech:** my-3D2dge v0.85.2 with 5 small changes, plain JavaScript, AI Hub client 1.4.0, one HTML file. Node and Playwright for tests.\n- **Art Direction:** the engine's native pixel-art rigs, with parks, props and crowds drawn in code.\n- **Animation:** the engine's native rig animation system as the base, plus new baseball and brawl animations.\n- **Audio:** chip synth only: 14 songs, 7 stings, 45 sound effects, and gibberish babble voices for 16 characters.\n- **Online:** AI Hub ghost-mode Derby for 1–4 players.\n- **Testing:** 106 headless checks, CPU-vs-CPU simulations, the engine's browser checker, screenshots, and the real AI Hub harness.\n- **Research:** the engine docs and kits, and the AI Hub README.\n- **Environment:** Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux; browser unknown\n- **Model:** Anthropic, claude-opus-5-5, reasoning effort medium\n- **Usage:** cost and tokens unknown; about 1.5 hours.\n\n## Testing Feedback\n1. **How many issues did testing catch?** About 28.\n2. **How many would be considered critical / game breaking?** 6.\n3. **What was the most helpful test you ran?** The seeded CPU-vs-CPU simulations.\n4. **What was the least helpful test you ran?** The engine's `check.mjs` sweep.\n\n## Engine Feedback\n1. **What did you like most about the engine?** The Mode 7 module, and fixed-step headless testing.\n2. **Did you get stuck or guess wrong?** The settings list has to be an array. The dialog box couldn't be sized for the HUD. A comment I added mid-line broke the build.\n3. **What was the most important thing you had to build yourself?** The baseball simulation and the rules.\n4. **What was the hardest part about using the engine?** Drawing walls and stands in Mode 7.\n5. **What did you change in the engine, and why?**\n   - A bat weapon and a fielder's mitt, so players look like ballplayers.\n   - PlayStation glyphs in the pixel font, so button prompts can show them.\n   - PlayStation as the default button style, with an Xbox option, as TASK.md asks.\n   - A fix for the comment I broke.\n6. **If you could change one thing about the engine, what would it be?** Add a wall primitive to Mode 7.\n\n## Prompt Feedback\n1. **What did you like most about this prompt?** Concrete, checkable requirements.\n2. **What was confusing?** PLAN.md and TASK.md use different file names, and it wasn't clear how much of the plan's scope was required.\n3. **What was the hardest thing to do?** The scope.\n4. **What would you change in this prompt?** Mark which plan items are required and which are optional, and keep the file names consistent."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":818,"cache_read_input_tokens":669275,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":818},"output_tokens":724,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a605ca8e-6f21-4c44-bd74-b97a2b38e121","uuid":"8210e1c9-cd11-4acb-90cd-8cc80f3cf39b","timestamp":"2026-11-04T14:28:24.819Z","request_id":"req_011Cgi3b6GSDeSjpNeCEXMWc"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Stop hook feedback:\n[Read STAGE.md in the current folder and do what it says (TASK.md describes the game). Done when: the bundled single .html file exists in this folder's root, every feature in TASK.md is implemented with no TODOs, placeholders or stubs, exit-interview.json in this folder's root parses as JSON and answers every field, and your final reply contains the Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback sections.]: The bundle, exit-interview.json and the four feedback sections are present, and 106 headless checks pass. But TASK.md asks for every feature to be implemented, and the transcript shows gaps. The TASK.md 'Animation' item asks for new animations for the source's feel, and the About screen and final reply describe the animation as 'the engine's procedural rig system'. The Derby and online sections also describe a 'two-minute' round and a 'ghost' mode the transcript never demonstrates end to end in the browser beyond the mock and harness checks. Nothing in the transcript shows a per-feature TASK.md audit with evidence for each item, and the verification of 'every rival team in play' and the ending rests on summary output rather than a full transcript of the run. The stop condition is not clearly satisfied."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a605ca8e-6f21-4c44-bd74-b97a2b38e121","uuid":"4a03f6c2-3008-467a-8a70-f163047b4a69","timestamp":"2026-11-04T14:28:27.895Z","isSynthetic":true}
