{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgi3gMgn9DGM38FPSxJVh","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Every TASK.md item is implemented and checked. The real AI Hub harness passed all three scenarios again in a browser. The animation gallery also rendered, showing the eleven new baseball and brawl animations.\n\n| TASK.md item | Evidence from this session |\n|---|---|\n| Single HTML in this folder's root | `ls work/` shows the game's .html and `exit-interview.json` next to STAGE.md. The hub client is the first script and is unchanged; there are no external requests. |\n| Genre, perspective, title by random draw | Screenshots of the Mode 7 plate view in all six parks, the field view and the home-run chase camera. The title came from the plan's random draw. |\n| Built on the engine; engine may change | Five changes, listed in `ENGINE-CHANGES.md`. |\n| Art: engine style plus new assets | Code-drawn parks, props, crowds and mascots (screenshots). |\n| Animation: engine system as the base, new animations | Gallery screenshot showing swing, bunt, pitch, throw, catcher, dive, slide, climb, punch, cheer and umpire. These run in play too (the brawl screenshot). |\n| Audio in code, gibberish voices | Synth songs, sound effects and per-letter babble voices. |\n| Online (AI Hub) | Real harness, end to end in Chromium, three times: \"3 passed, 0 failed\". It covered 2 players; 4 players with latency, jitter and loss; and the host leaving. Mock checks cover the ghost round's card, progress, result, time-up and ghost comets. |\n| Multiplayer on its own | \"PASS a four-player exhibition finishes\", \"a second player joins\", \"the co-captain runs the bases\". |\n| Feature-complete demo | Full Tour: \"stop 1 … stop 5 plays to the results\", \"the scripted Rhubarb at Caldera Field\", \"the Tour ends: credits, everything unlocked\". All six parks and teams reach results with 0 errors. The 8 lessons, the Derby, pickoffs and replays all pass. |\n| Dev mode, sliders, reset | \"PASS a slider moves TUNE\", \"reset to defaults\", \"a cheat toggles\", \"the situation applies\". |\n| Attract mode | \"10 s idle on the title starts the attract mode\", \"every segment runs and the reel loops\", \"any input returns to the title\". |\n| Narrative tone | Radio-style commentary pools: \"6+ lines, none over 100 chars\". |\n| 10-foot UI, PlayStation glyphs, Xbox option, native keyboard and mouse | \"PlayStation glyphs by default\", \"the Xbox setting shows A B X Y\", \"keyboard prompts show keys\", \"mouse prompts show buttons\". Screenshots show the ✕ and A icons. |\n| Touch-only devices | \"touch-only shows the card\", \"attract runs on touch-only devices\". |\n| No TODOs, placeholders or stubs | 0 matches in the game code. |\n| About/Credits screen with the four sections | \"every Source Information field filled\", \"feedback sections sized 4/6/4\". |\n| `exit-interview.json` | Parses, with no empty values. |\n| Testing | `node tests/run.mjs`: 106 passed, 0 failed, every line printed. |\n\n\"Unknown\" appears only for cost and tokens. TASK.md line 59 asks for \"unknown\" for anything that can't be confirmed, and line 73 wants usage only if estimates are available. No usage meter was available.\n\n## Source Information\n- **Date:** 2026-11-04 06:01:14\n- **Source:** Baseball (the sport), over-the-top arcade style\n- **Plan:** PLAN.md\n- **Genre and Perspective:** arcade baseball, with a slapstick brawl mini-game and a story Tour. A Mode 7 plate view behind the catcher, a three-quarter field view, and a home-run chase camera.\n- **Tech:** my-3D2dge v0.85.2 with 5 small changes, plain JavaScript, the AI Hub client 1.4.0, one HTML file. Tested with Node and Playwright.\n- **Art Direction:** the engine's native pixel-art rigs, with code-drawn parks, props and crowds.\n- **Animation:** the engine's native rig animation system as the base, plus new baseball and brawl animations.\n- **Audio:** chip synth only: 14 songs, 7 stings, 45 sound effects, and babble voices for 16 characters.\n- **Online:** AI Hub ghost-mode Derby for 1–4 players.\n- **Testing:** 106 headless checks, CPU-vs-CPU simulations, the engine's browser checker, screenshots, and the real AI Hub harness.\n- **Research:** the engine docs and kits, and the AI Hub README.\n- **Environment:** Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux; browser unknown\n- **Model:** Anthropic, claude-opus-5-5, reasoning effort medium\n- **Usage:** cost and tokens unknown; session time about 1.5 hours.\n\n## Testing Feedback\n1. **How many issues did testing catch?** About 28.\n2. **How many would be considered critical / game breaking?** 6.\n3. **What was the most helpful test you ran?** The seeded CPU-vs-CPU simulations.\n4. **What was the least helpful test you ran?** The engine's `check.mjs` sweep.\n\n## Engine Feedback\n1. **What did you like most about the engine?** The Mode 7 module and fixed-step headless testing.\n2. **Did you get stuck or guess wrong?** Settings must be an array. The dialog box can't be sized for the HUD. A comment I added mid-line broke the build.\n3. **What was the most important thing you had to build yourself?** The baseball simulation and the rules.\n4. **What was the hardest part about using the engine?** Drawing walls and stands in Mode 7.\n5. **What did you change in the engine, and why?**\n   - A bat weapon and a mitt, so players can swing a bat and wear a glove.\n   - PlayStation glyphs in the font, because the font couldn't draw them.\n   - PlayStation as the default button-symbol setting, with an Xbox option, as TASK.md asks.\n   - A fix for the mid-line comment I broke.\n6. **If you could change one thing about the engine, what would it be?** Add a wall primitive to Mode 7.\n\n## Prompt Feedback\n1. **What did you like most about this prompt?** Concrete, checkable requirements.\n2. **What was confusing?** PLAN.md and TASK.md use different file names, and it wasn't clear how much of the plan's scope was required.\n3. **What was the hardest thing to do?** The scope.\n4. **What would you change in this prompt?** Mark which items are required and which are optional, and keep the names consistent."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":249,"cache_read_input_tokens":674889,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":249},"output_tokens":763,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a605ca8e-6f21-4c44-bd74-b97a2b38e121","uuid":"44245c01-8c20-4353-ad65-f871b15ef350","timestamp":"2026-11-04T14:29:40.574Z","request_id":"req_011Cgi3gMHTbXhwvx4iqHEJK"}
