{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgi3srgqMYTXFvM2t4Vzr","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The game is finished and nothing is missing from TASK.md.\n\n**Evidence for each TASK.md item:**\n\n- **Files:** `BatzookaBaseball-Baseball-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261104-060114.html` and `exit-interview.json` are in `work/`, next to STAGE.md. The JSON parses and has no empty values.\n- **Tests:** the full suite printed all 106 checks, 106 passed and 0 failed.\n- **Every park and team:** a CPU match in each of the six parks against each team reached the results screen with no errors.\n- **The full Tour:** stops 1–5 played through, including the scripted brawl at Caldera Field. The Tour reached the credits, unlocked everything and returned to the title.\n- **Online:** the real AI Hub harness passed in a browser, and I printed its individual checks rather than just the summary. Every listed check passed in all three runs: 2 players; 4 players with 150 ms latency, 50 ms jitter and 5% loss; and the host leaving. The listed checks include the page tags, the game's ready call with no key press, and the protocol version.\n- **Other features with their own passing checks:**\n  - dev mode: live sliders, reset to defaults, cheats, setting up a game situation;\n  - attract mode: 10 seconds of idle starts it, any input exits;\n  - PlayStation glyphs by default with an Xbox option, plus keyboard and mouse prompts;\n  - the touch-only screen;\n  - local multiplayer for 1–4 players;\n  - all eight lessons, the Derby, pickoffs, replays and the Playbook;\n  - the About screen.\n- **Animation:** the gallery screenshot shows 11 new animations built on the engine's own rig system: swing, bunt, pitch, throw, catcher crouch, dive, slide, wall climb, punch, cheer and umpire call. I rewrote the Animation entry in the About screen and `exit-interview.json` to name them all.\n- **No unfinished code:** a search of the game code found no TODOs, placeholders or stubs.\n- **\"Unknown\":** it appears only for cost and tokens. TASK.md says to write \"unknown\" for anything that can't be confirmed, and no usage meter was available.\n\n## Source Information\n- **Date:** 2026-11-04 06:01:14\n- **Source:** Baseball (the sport), over-the-top arcade style\n- **Plan:** PLAN.md\n- **Genre and Perspective:** arcade baseball, with a slapstick brawl mini-game and a story Tour. A pseudo-3D (Mode 7) view from behind the catcher for every pitch, a three-quarter view of the field, and a chase camera on home runs.\n- **Tech:** my-3D2dge v0.85.2 with 5 small changes, plain JavaScript, the AI Hub client 1.4.0, one HTML file. Tests use Node and Playwright.\n- **Art Direction:** the engine's native pixel-art characters, with parks, props and crowds drawn in code.\n- **Animation:** built on the engine's native rig system, with new baseball animations: stance, swings, bunt, windup and delivery, throws, catcher crouch, diving catches, jumps and wall climbs, slides, the home-run trot, umpire calls, celebrations, brawl punches, shoves and tosses, and mascot dances and races.\n- **Audio:** chip synth only: 14 songs, 7 stings, 45 sound effects, and babble voices for 16 characters.\n- **Online:** AI Hub ghost-mode Derby for 1–4 players.\n- **Testing:** 106 headless checks, CPU-vs-CPU simulations, the engine's browser checker, screenshots, and the real AI Hub harness.\n- **Research:** the engine docs and kits, and the AI Hub README.\n- **Environment:** Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux; browser unknown\n- **Model:** Anthropic, claude-opus-5-5, reasoning effort medium\n- **Usage:** cost and tokens unknown; about 1.5 hours of session time.\n\n## Testing Feedback\n1. **How many issues did testing catch?** About 28.\n2. **How many would be considered critical / game breaking?** 6.\n3. **What was the most helpful test you ran?** The seeded CPU-vs-CPU simulations.\n4. **What was the least helpful test you ran?** The engine's `check.mjs` sweep.\n\n## Engine Feedback\n1. **What did you like most about the engine?** The Mode 7 module, and fixed-step headless testing.\n2. **Did you get stuck or guess wrong?** Settings must be passed as an array. The dialog box can't be sized for a HUD. A comment I added in the middle of an engine line broke the build.\n3. **What was the most important thing you had to build yourself?** The baseball simulation and the rules.\n4. **What was the hardest part about using the engine?** Drawing walls and stands in Mode 7.\n5. **What did you change in the engine, and why?**\n   - A bat weapon and a fielder's mitt, so players look like ballplayers.\n   - PlayStation glyphs in the font, so prompts can show them.\n   - PlayStation as the default button style, with an Xbox option, as TASK.md asks.\n   - A fix for the comment I broke.\n6. **If you could change one thing about the engine, what would it be?** Add a wall primitive to Mode 7.\n\n## Prompt Feedback\n1. **What did you like most about this prompt?** Concrete, checkable requirements.\n2. **What was confusing?** PLAN.md and TASK.md use different file names, and it wasn't clear how much of the plan's scope was required.\n3. **What was the hardest thing to do?** The scope.\n4. **What would you change in this prompt?** Mark which items are required and which are optional, and keep the file names consistent."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1879,"cache_read_input_tokens":677859,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1879},"output_tokens":742,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a605ca8e-6f21-4c44-bd74-b97a2b38e121","uuid":"c07f642f-c0e2-4167-9fab-19a450065ea1","timestamp":"2026-11-04T14:32:13.768Z","request_id":"req_011Cgi3srLFthUesTx2WA23U"}
