{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgi3wM8hi9CS6uXKAdKpC","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The game is finished. I wrote `AUDIT.md` in the dev folder, which checks every TASK.md requirement one by one. Every row points to the code that implements it and to a check or screenshot from this session.\n\n- **Requirements (28 rows):** all are implemented, including the art and animation, online play, dev mode, attract mode, touch-only devices, the About screen and `exit-interview.json`. The last runs were 106 of 106 checks passed, and all three AI Hub harness scenarios passed. Every rival team, the full Tour and the ending were also played through.\n- **Animation (row 9):** the new baseball motions are the stance, swings, bunt, windup, throws, catcher's crouch, dives, jumps, wall climbs, slides, the home-run trot and celebrations. The brawl adds punches, shoves, tosses and knockdowns, and the mascots race and dance.\n- **Playbook:** it was never missing. It opens from the pause menu and turns pages; that check passed earlier in this session.\n- **Issue counts:** the audit lists all 28 issues the tests caught, each with what caught it: 12 code bugs, 1 balance problem and 15 layout fixes. Six of them were critical.\n\nThe game file and `exit-interview.json` are in `work/`, next to STAGE.md. The JSON parses with no empty fields, and the game code contains no TODOs, placeholders or stubs.\n\n## Source Information\n- **Date:** 2026-11-04 06:01:14\n- **Source:** Baseball (the sport), over-the-top arcade style\n- **Plan:** PLAN.md\n- **Genre and Perspective:** Arcade baseball, with a slapstick brawl mini-game and a story Tour. A pseudo-3D (Mode 7) plate view from behind the catcher, a three-quarter field view, and a chase camera for home runs.\n- **Tech:** my-3D2dge v0.85.2 with 5 small changes, plain JavaScript, AI Hub client 1.4.0, one HTML file. Node and Playwright for tests.\n- **Art Direction:** The engine's native pixel-art characters, with parks, props and crowds drawn in code.\n- **Animation:** Built on the engine's native rig system, with new baseball and brawl animations (listed in `AUDIT.md` row 9 and shown in the in-game Animation Gallery).\n- **Audio:** Chip synth only: 14 songs, 7 stings, 45 sound effects, and babble voices for 16 characters.\n- **Online:** AI Hub ghost-mode Derby for 1–4 players.\n- **Testing:** 106 headless checks, CPU-vs-CPU simulations, the engine's browser checker, screenshots, and the real AI Hub harness.\n- **Research:** The engine docs and kits, and the AI Hub README.\n- **Environment:** Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux; browser unknown\n- **Model:** Anthropic, claude-opus-5-5, reasoning effort medium\n- **Usage:** Cost and tokens unknown; about 1.5 hours.\n\n## Testing Feedback\n1. **How many issues did testing catch?** About 28: 12 code bugs, 1 balance problem and 15 layout problems, each listed in `AUDIT.md`.\n2. **How many would be considered critical / game breaking?** 6: two syntax errors, two frozen games (pitch speed came out as NaN), a crash on contact when no fielders were placed, and late swings counting as strikes.\n3. **What was the most helpful test you ran?** The seeded CPU-vs-CPU simulations.\n4. **What was the least helpful test you ran?** The engine's `check.mjs` sweep.\n\n## Engine Feedback\n1. **What did you like most about the engine?** Mode 7, and headless fixed-step testing.\n2. **Did you get stuck or guess wrong?** Settings must be an array. The dialog box can't be sized for a HUD. A comment I added mid-line broke the build.\n3. **What was the most important thing you had to build yourself?** The baseball simulation and the rules.\n4. **What was the hardest part about using the engine?** Drawing walls and stands in Mode 7.\n5. **What did you change in the engine, and why?**\n   - Added a bat and a mitt, so players look like ballplayers.\n   - Added PlayStation glyphs to the font, so prompts can show them.\n   - Made PlayStation the default glyph setting, with an Xbox option.\n   - Fixed the comment I broke.\n6. **If you could change one thing about the engine, what would it be?** Add a wall primitive to Mode 7.\n\n## Prompt Feedback\n1. **What did you like most about this prompt?** Concrete, checkable requirements.\n2. **What was confusing?** PLAN.md and TASK.md use different file names, and the plan's scope was unclear.\n3. **What was the hardest thing to do?** The scope.\n4. **What would you change in this prompt?** Mark which items are required and which are optional, and keep the names consistent."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3056,"cache_read_input_tokens":682075,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3056},"output_tokens":754,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a605ca8e-6f21-4c44-bd74-b97a2b38e121","uuid":"389abf0f-aac7-48cd-86aa-76d84efdbec0","timestamp":"2026-11-04T14:32:58.772Z","request_id":"req_011Cgi3wLmsLKX1HH3UGfs87"}
