{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgi3z5D5AWPweypiTYohF","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The game is finished, and I now have the AI Hub results check by check rather than as a summary. All 16 harness checks passed in the hardest scenario: 4 players with 150 ms latency, 50 ms jitter and 5% packet loss. The 2-player and host-leaves runs also passed, but those runs printed only their summaries.\n\n**Evidence already printed in this session:**\n- **Tour:** the stop 1–5 PASS lines, the scripted brawl at Caldera Field, the ending reaching the credits with everything unlocked, and the return to the title.\n- **Every park and team:** the six-park run, where each match reached the results screen with 0 errors.\n- **Full test suite:** 106 of 106 checks passed, each printed.\n- **Animations:** the gallery screenshot, plus the new animation code (`SWING_SPEC`, `BUNT_SPEC`, `PITCH_SPEC` and the brawl combos) shown above.\n- **Issue counts:** `AUDIT.md` lists the 28 issues by name and what caught each one; each came from a failing run or screenshot during this session.\n- **Files:** the game and `exit-interview.json` are in the STAGE.md folder, and the JSON parses with no empty fields.\n\n## Source Information\n- **Date:** 2026-11-04 06:01:14\n- **Source:** Baseball (the sport), over-the-top arcade style\n- **Plan:** PLAN.md\n- **Genre and Perspective:** Arcade baseball, plus a slapstick brawl mini-game and a story Tour. A pseudo-3D (Mode 7) camera behind the catcher for pitching and batting, a three-quarter view for play in the field, and a chase camera for home runs.\n- **Tech:** my-3D2dge v0.85.2 (5 small changes), plain JavaScript, AI Hub client 1.4.0, one HTML file. Node and Playwright for testing.\n- **Art Direction:** The engine's native pixel-art characters, with code-drawn parks, props and crowds.\n- **Animation:** The engine's native rig system as the base, plus new baseball and brawl animations.\n- **Audio:** Chip synth only: 14 songs, 7 stings, 45 sound effects, and gibberish (Animalese-style) voices for 16 characters.\n- **Online:** AI Hub ghost-mode Derby for 1–4 players.\n- **Testing:** 106 headless checks, CPU-vs-CPU simulations, the engine's browser checker, screenshots, and the real AI Hub harness.\n- **Research:** The engine's docs and starter kits, and the AI Hub README.\n- **Environment:** Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux; browser unknown\n- **Model:** Anthropic, claude-opus-5-5, reasoning effort medium\n- **Usage:** Cost and tokens unknown; about 1.5 hours.\n\n## Testing Feedback\n1. **How many issues did testing catch?** About 28: 12 code bugs, 1 balance problem and 15 layout problems.\n2. **How many would be considered critical / game breaking?** 6.\n3. **What was the most helpful test you ran?** The seeded CPU-vs-CPU simulations.\n4. **What was the least helpful test you ran?** The engine's `check.mjs` sweep.\n\n## Engine Feedback\n1. **What did you like most about the engine?** Mode 7, and headless fixed-step testing.\n2. **Did you get stuck or guess wrong?** Settings had to be an array, the dialog box couldn't be sized for the HUD, and a comment I added mid-line broke the build.\n3. **What was the most important thing you had to build yourself?** The baseball simulation and the rules.\n4. **What was the hardest part about using the engine?** Drawing walls and stands in Mode 7.\n5. **What did you change in the engine, and why?**\n   - Added a bat and a mitt, so players look like ballplayers.\n   - Added PlayStation button glyphs to the font, so prompts can show them.\n   - Made PlayStation glyphs the default, with an Xbox option.\n   - Fixed the comment I broke.\n6. **If you could change one thing about the engine, what would it be?** Add a wall primitive to Mode 7.\n\n## Prompt Feedback\n1. **What did you like most about this prompt?** Concrete, checkable requirements.\n2. **What was confusing?** PLAN.md and TASK.md use different file names, and it wasn't clear how much of the plan's scope was required.\n3. **What was the hardest thing to do?** The scope.\n4. **What would you change in this prompt?** Mark which items are required and which are optional, and keep the names consistent."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":835,"cache_read_input_tokens":687169,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":835},"output_tokens":796,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a605ca8e-6f21-4c44-bd74-b97a2b38e121","uuid":"1c34bb47-9b38-4e5b-a2d5-fdadf4887bbf","timestamp":"2026-11-04T14:33:34.804Z","request_id":"req_011Cgi3z4n2umnA4SF7i1jLd"}
