{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgi43HvtNa2NeDkh2nvWY","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I printed both remaining AI Hub harness runs check by check, and both passed every check. All three scenarios now have full output: 2 players, 4 players over a lossy network (shown in the previous run), and the host leaving. Each passed all 16 protocol checks.\n\nThe Tour stops, the ending, and every park with its rival team were also shown as individual pass lines earlier in this session. The last full suite run passed all 106 checks. Nothing changed since that run apart from the about text and test-tool printing, so I have nothing further to add: every TASK.md feature is implemented, and `AUDIT.md` in the dev folder maps each one to its code and proof.\n\nThe game and `exit-interview.json` are both in the STAGE.md folder:\n- `BatzookaBaseball-Baseball-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261104-060114.html`\n- `exit-interview.json`\n\n## Source Information\n- **Date:** 2026-11-04 06:01:14\n- **Source:** Baseball (the sport), over-the-top arcade style\n- **Plan:** PLAN.md\n- **Genre and Perspective:** Arcade baseball, plus a slapstick brawl mini-game and a story Tour. The camera is a Mode 7 view from behind the catcher for every pitch, a three-quarter view of the field for play after contact, and a chase camera on home runs.\n- **Tech:** my-3D2dge v0.85.2 (5 small engine changes), plain JavaScript, AI Hub client 1.4.0, all in one HTML file. Node and Playwright for testing.\n- **Art Direction:** The engine's native pixel-art characters; parks, props and crowds drawn in code.\n- **Animation:** The engine's native rig system as the base, plus new baseball and brawl animations.\n- **Audio:** All from the engine's chip synth: 14 songs, 7 stings, 45 sound effects, and gibberish babble voices for 16 characters.\n- **Online:** AI Hub Derby in ghost mode, 1–4 players.\n- **Testing:**\n  - 106 headless checks\n  - CPU-vs-CPU simulations\n  - the engine's browser checker\n  - screenshots\n  - the real AI Hub harness (3 scenarios, 16 checks each, all passing)\n- **Research:** The engine docs and kits, and the AI Hub README.\n- **Environment:** Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux; browser unknown\n- **Model:** Anthropic, claude-opus-5-5, reasoning effort medium\n- **Usage:** Cost and tokens unknown; about 1.5 hours.\n\n## Testing Feedback\n1. **How many issues did testing catch?** About 28: 12 code bugs, 1 balance problem and 15 layout problems.\n2. **How many were critical or game-breaking?** 6.\n3. **Most helpful test:** the seeded CPU-vs-CPU simulations.\n4. **Least helpful test:** the engine's `check.mjs` sweep.\n\n## Engine Feedback\n1. **What did you like most?** The Mode 7 module and headless fixed-step testing.\n2. **Did you get stuck or guess wrong?**\n   - Settings have to be an array.\n   - The dialog box can't be sized for a HUD.\n   - A comment I added mid-line broke the build.\n3. **Most important thing you built yourself:** the baseball simulation and its rules.\n4. **Hardest part of using the engine:** drawing walls and stands in Mode 7.\n5. **What did you change in the engine, and why?**\n   - Added a bat and a fielder's mitt, so players look like ballplayers.\n   - Added PlayStation button glyphs to the font, because the font couldn't draw them.\n   - Made PlayStation glyphs the default, with an Xbox option, as TASK.md asks.\n   - Fixed the comment I broke.\n6. **One thing you'd change:** add a wall primitive to Mode 7.\n\n## Prompt Feedback\n1. **What did you like most?** Concrete, checkable requirements.\n2. **What was confusing?** The file names differ between PLAN.md and TASK.md, and it wasn't clear how much of the plan's scope was required.\n3. **Hardest thing to do:** fitting the scope into one session.\n4. **What would you change?** Mark which items are required and which are optional, and keep the file names consistent."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_se