ght.\n- **Art Direction:** the engine's native pixel-art characters, with parks, props and crowds drawn in code.\n- **Animation:** the engine's native rig system as the base, plus new baseball and brawl animations.\n- **Audio:** chip synth only — 14 songs, 7 short jingles, 45 sound effects, and gibberish babble voices for 16 characters.\n- **Online:** AI Hub ghost-mode Derby for 1–4 players.\n- **Testing:** 106 headless checks, CPU-vs-CPU simulations, the engine's browser checker, screenshots, and the real AI Hub harness.\n- **Research:** the engine's docs and starter kits, and the AI Hub README.\n- **Environment:** Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux; browser unknown\n- **Model:** Anthropic, claude-opus-5-5, reasoning effort medium\n- **Usage:** cost and tokens unknown; about 1.5 hours.\n\n## Testing Feedback\n1. **How many issues did testing catch?** About 28: 12 code bugs, 1 balance problem and 15 layout problems.\n2. **How many would be considered critical / game breaking?** 6.\n3. **What was the most helpful test you ran?** The seeded CPU-vs-CPU simulations.\n4. **What was the least helpful test you ran?** The engine's `check.mjs` sweep.\n\n## Engine Feedback\n1. **What did you like most about the engine?** Mode 7, and headless testing with fixed time steps.\n2. **Did you get stuck or guess wrong?**\n   - The settings list must be an array.\n   - The dialog box can't be sized to fit a HUD.\n   - A comment I added in the middle of an engine line broke the build.\n3. **What was the most important thing you had to build yourself?** The baseball simulation and its rules.\n4. **What was the hardest part about using the engine?** Drawing walls and stands in Mode 7.\n5. **What did you change in the engine, and why?**\n   - Added a bat and a mitt so players look like ballplayers.\n   - Added PlayStation button symbols to the font so prompts can show them.\n   - Made PlayStation symbols the default, with an Xbox option, as TASK.md asks.\n   - Fixed the comment I broke.\n6. **If you could change one thing about the engine, what would it be?** Add a wall primitive to Mode 7.\n\n## Prompt Feedback\n1. **What did you like most about this prompt?** Concrete, checkable requirements.\n2. **What was confusing?** PLAN.md and TASK.md use different file names, and it wasn't clear how much of the plan's scope was required.\n3. **What was the hardest thing to do?** Fitting the scope into one session.\n4. **What would you change in this prompt?** Mark which items are required and which are optional, and keep the file names consistent."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2138,"cache_read_input_tokens":692623,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2138},"output_tokens":9,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a605ca8e-6f21-4c44-bd74-b97a2b38e121","uuid":"2914c425-5a74-4036-8c0d-52254a456fc6","timestamp":"2026-11-04T14:34:53.465Z","request_id":"req_011Cgi45fu3P8xBn5SKz56yF"}
