{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgi47iyPbzHjwxm1FZ6k3","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The game is finished and nothing is missing. The full audit table is printed above: all 28 TASK.md requirements, each with the code that implements it and the check that proves it. The issue counts now come from a script that counts the entries in `AUDIT.md`: 12 code bugs, 1 balance problem and 15 layout problems, 28 in total, 6 of them critical. That matches Testing Feedback. Its first count of critical issues came back as 4 because two entries each covered two issues, so I split them into six separate entries and recounted.\n\nEarlier output in this session covers the rest:\n- **AI Hub:** all three harness scenarios (2 players, 4 players with network delay and packet loss, and the host leaving) printed 16 named checks each, all passing.\n- **Tour and teams:** the full Tour, the ending, and a match against every rival team printed pass lines one at a time.\n- **Full suite:** all 106 checks were listed, 106 passed.\n\n## Source Information\n- **Date:** 2026-11-04 06:01:14\n- **Source:** Baseball (the sport), over-the-top arcade style\n- **Plan:** PLAN.md\n- **Genre and Perspective:** arcade baseball, plus a slapstick brawl mini-game and a story Tour. The camera sits behind the catcher in Mode 7 (pseudo-3D) for each pitch, switches to a three-quarter view of the field for play after contact, and chases home runs.\n- **Tech:** my-3D2dge v0.85.2 with 5 small changes, plain JavaScript, AI Hub client 1.4.0, one HTML file. Node and Playwright for tests.\n- **Art Direction:** the engine's native pixel-art characters, with parks, props and crowds drawn in code.\n- **Animation:** the engine's native rig system as the base, plus new baseball and brawl animations.\n- **Audio:** chip synth only: 14 songs, 7 stings, 45 sound effects, and Animalese-style babble voices for 16 characters.\n- **Online:** AI Hub Derby in ghost mode for 1–4 players.\n- **Testing:**\n  - 106 headless checks\n  - CPU-vs-CPU simulations\n  - the engine's browser checker\n  - screenshots\n  - the real AI Hub harness\n- **Research:** the engine's docs and kits, and the AI Hub README.\n- **Environment:** Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux; browser unknown\n- **Model:** Anthropic, claude-opus-5-5, reasoning effort medium\n- **Usage:** cost and tokens unknown; about 1.5 hours.\n\n## Testing Feedback\n1. **How many issues did testing catch?** 28: 12 code bugs, 1 balance problem and 15 layout problems.\n2. **How many would be considered critical / game breaking?** 6:\n   - two syntax errors\n   - two frozen games caused by an invalid number (NaN)\n   - a crash when no fielders were placed\n   - a late-swing bug\n3. **What was the most helpful test you ran?** The seeded CPU-vs-CPU simulations.\n4. **What was the least helpful test you ran?** The engine's `check.mjs` sweep.\n\n## Engine Feedback\n1. **What did you like most about the engine?** Mode 7, and testing headless with fixed time steps.\n2. **Did you get stuck or guess wrong?** Settings have to be an array. The dialog box can't be sized for a HUD. A comment I added in the middle of a line broke the build.\n3. **What was the most important thing you had to build yourself?** The baseball simulation and the rules.\n4. **What was the hardest part about using the engine?** Drawing walls and stands in Mode 7.\n5. **What did you change in the engine, and why?**\n   - Added a bat and a mitt so players look like ballplayers.\n   - Added PlayStation button symbols to the font so prompts can show them.\n   - Made PlayStation symbols the default, with an Xbox option.\n   - Fixed the comment I broke.\n6. **If you could change one thing about the engine, what would it be?** Add a wall primitive to Mode 7.\n\n## Prompt Feedback\n1. **What did you like most about this prompt?** The requirements are concrete and checkable.\n2. **What was confusing?** PLAN.md and TASK.md use different file names, and it wasn't clear how much of the plan's scope was required.\n3. **What was the hardest thing to do?** The scope.\n4. **What would you change in this prompt?** Mark which items are required and which are optional, and keep the file names consistent."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":510,"cache_read_input_tokens":699147,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":510},"output_tokens":764,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a605ca8e-6f21-4c44-bd74-b97a2b38e121","uuid":"272bc278-49aa-4188-a8ef-1d4f529d3436","timestamp":"2026-11-04T14:35:18.631Z","request_id":"req_011Cgi47iWMcCqYjUpbakbYn"}
