{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgi49e3GjdUKFgHgqpD3W","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I recorded 12 frames of the animation gallery at quarter speed. Across them, the new motions move from frame to frame: the swing winds up and follows through, the pitcher delivers, the fielder throws, the diver goes down, the runner slides, the climber goes up the wall, the punch lands and the umpire makes his call. TASK.md's animation requirement asks for the engine's own system with new animations made for the source. That is what the game does, and these frames show it in motion.\n\nThat was the last evidence still missing. The rest is printed earlier in this session:\n- **Requirements audit:** all 28 TASK.md requirements, with the code that implements each and how it was checked.\n- **Issue tally:** counted by a script — 12 code bugs, 1 balance problem, 15 layout problems, 28 in total, 6 of them critical.\n- **Test suite:** all 106 checks, every one passing.\n- **Tour and rivals:** the full Tour including the ending, and a match against every rival team.\n- **AI Hub:** all 16 named checks passing in each of the three harness scenarios.\n\nThe game and `exit-interview.json` are in the folder with STAGE.md, and the JSON parses.\n\n## Source Information\n- **Date:** 2026-11-04 06:01:14\n- **Source:** Baseball (the sport), over-the-top arcade style\n- **Plan:** PLAN.md\n- **Genre and Perspective:** Arcade baseball, with a slapstick brawl mini-game and a story Tour. The camera sits behind the catcher in a Mode 7 pseudo-3D view for each pitch, switches to a three-quarter view of the field for play after contact, and chases the ball on home runs.\n- **Tech:** my-3D2dge v0.85.2 with 5 small changes, plain JavaScript, AI Hub client 1.4.0, one HTML file. Node and Playwright for tests.\n- **Art Direction:** The engine's native pixel-art characters, with parks, props and crowds drawn in code.\n- **Animation:** The engine's native rig system as the base, plus new baseball and brawl animations.\n- **Audio:** Chip synth only: 14 songs, 7 stings, 45 sound effects, and babble voices for 16 characters.\n- **Online:** AI Hub ghost-mode Derby for 1–4 players.\n- **Testing:** 106 headless checks, CPU-vs-CPU simulations, the engine's browser checker, screenshots and filmstrips, and the real AI Hub harness.\n- **Research:** The engine's docs and starter kits, and the AI Hub README.\n- **Environment:** Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux; browser unknown\n- **Model:** Anthropic, claude-opus-5-5, reasoning effort medium\n- **Usage:** Cost and tokens unknown; about 1.5 hours.\n\n## Testing Feedback\n1. **How many issues did testing catch?** 28: 12 code bugs, 1 balance problem and 15 layout problems.\n2. **How many would be considered critical / game breaking?** 6:\n   - two syntax errors\n   - two games that froze because a value became NaN\n   - a crash when no fielders were placed\n   - a bug in late swings\n3. **What was the most helpful test you ran?** The seeded CPU-vs-CPU simulations.\n4. **What was the least helpful test you ran?** The engine's `check.mjs` sweep.\n\n## Engine Feedback\n1. **What did you like most about the engine?** Mode 7, and headless testing with fixed time steps.\n2. **Did you get stuck or guess wrong?** Settings must be an array. The dialog box can't be sized to fit a HUD. A comment I added in the middle of a line broke the build.\n3. **What was the most important thing you had to build yourself?** The baseball simulation and its rules.\n4. **What was the hardest part about using the engine?** Drawing walls and stands in Mode 7.\n5. **What did you change in the engine, and why?**\n   - Added a bat and a mitt, so players look like ballplayers.\n   - Added PlayStation button glyphs to the font, so prompts can show them.\n   - Made PlayStation glyphs the default, with an Xbox option.\n   - Fixed the comment I broke.\n6. **If you could change one thing about the engine, what would it be?** Add a wall primitive to Mode 7.\n\n## Prompt Feedback\n1. **What did you like most about this prompt?** Concrete, checkable requirements.\n2. **What was confusing?** PLAN.md and TASK.md use different file names, and it wasn't clear how much of the plan's scope was required.\n3. **What was the hardest thing to do?** The scope.\n4. **What would you change in this prompt?** Mark which items are required and which are optional, and keep the names consistent."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":100,"cache_read_input_tokens":703076,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":100},"output_tokens":740,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a605ca8e-6f21-4c44-bd74-b97a2b38e121","uuid":"b3f8a2ca-da93-4d8d-ba06-619ef6e56063","timestamp":"2026-11-04T14:35:44.681Z","request_id":"req_011Cgi49dW34xd3E7Pa5Kt54"}
