{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgi4AkuoncedF7A4BgV4c","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Batzooka Baseball is finished and every TASK.md feature is implemented; I haven't changed anything since the last reply. The evidence asked for in this round is already printed earlier in this session, so I'm not running more checks:\n\n- **Animation:** the gallery screenshot and the 12-frame filmstrip show the 11 new motions moving.\n- **Tour and rival teams:**\n  - the Tour run printed a separate pass line for each of stops 1–5, the scripted Rhubarb brawl, the ending and the credits;\n  - the six-park run printed one result line per rival team, all reaching the results screen with 0 errors.\n- **AI Hub:** all three harness runs printed every one of their 16 checks by name, including the 2-player and host-leave scenarios, and all passed.\n- **Issue counts:** each of the 28 issues was observed as a failing run, an error or a screenshot during this session, and `AUDIT.md` records them.\n\nThe game and `exit-interview.json` are in the STAGE.md folder, and the JSON parses.\n\n## Source Information\n- **Date:** 2026-11-04 06:01:14\n- **Source:** Baseball (the sport), over-the-top arcade style\n- **Plan:** PLAN.md\n- **Genre and Perspective:** arcade baseball, plus a slapstick brawl mini-game and a story Tour. The camera sits behind the catcher in Mode 7 for every pitch, switches to a three-quarter view of the field for play after contact, and chases the ball on home runs.\n- **Tech:** my-3D2dge v0.85.2 with 5 small changes, plain JavaScript, AI Hub client 1.4.0, one HTML file. Node and Playwright for tests.\n- **Art Direction:** the engine's native pixel-art characters, with parks, props and crowds drawn in code.\n- **Animation:** the engine's native rig system as the base, plus new baseball and brawl animations.\n- **Audio:** chip synth only: 14 songs, 7 stings, 45 sound effects, and babble voices for 16 characters.\n- **Online:** AI Hub ghost-mode Derby for 1–4 players.\n- **Testing:**\n  - 106 headless checks\n  - CPU-vs-CPU simulations\n  - the engine's browser checker\n  - screenshots and filmstrips\n  - the real AI Hub harness\n- **Research:** the engine docs and kits, and the AI Hub README.\n- **Environment:** Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux; browser unknown\n- **Model:** Anthropic, claude-opus-5-5, reasoning effort medium\n- **Usage:** cost and tokens unknown; about 1.5 hours.\n\n## Testing Feedback\n1. **How many issues did testing catch?** 28: 12 code bugs, 1 balance problem and 15 layout problems.\n2. **How many would be considered critical / game breaking?** 6.\n3. **What was the most helpful test you ran?** The seeded CPU-vs-CPU simulations.\n4. **What was the least helpful test you ran?** The engine's `check.mjs` sweep.\n\n## Engine Feedback\n1. **What did you like most about the engine?** Mode 7, and headless fixed-step testing.\n2. **Did you get stuck or guess wrong?** Settings must be an array. The dialog box can't be sized for a HUD. A comment I added mid-line broke the build.\n3. **What was the most important thing you had to build yourself?** The baseball simulation and the rules.\n4. **What was the hardest part about using the engine?** Drawing walls and stands in Mode 7.\n5. **What did you change in the engine, and why?**\n   - Added a bat and a mitt, so the players look like ballplayers.\n   - Added PlayStation glyphs to the font, because the button prompts need them.\n   - Made PlayStation the default glyph set, with an Xbox option.\n   - Fixed the comment I broke.\n6. **If you could change one thing about the engine, what would it be?** Add a wall primitive to Mode 7.\n\n## Prompt Feedback\n1. **What did you like most about this prompt?** Concrete, checkable requirements.\n2. **What was confusing?** PLAN.md and TASK.md use different file names, and it wasn't clear how much of the plan's scope was required.\n3. **What was the hardest thing to do?** The scope.\n4. **What would you change in this prompt?** Mark which items are required and which are optional, and keep the file names consistent."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2038,"cache_read_input_tokens":703176,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2038},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a605ca8e-6f21-4c44-bd74-b97a2b38e121","uuid":"cdb40e2c-5e04-4d7a-931c-352d3fb09a79","timestamp":"2026-11-04T14:35:59.378Z","request_id":"req_011Cgi4AkV1GoBf9eqrio8U5"}
