{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgi4SMoC5CeNjks6Q9ttd","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I reran everything just now and printed every result.\n\n- **Full test suite:** 106 of 106 checks passed. They cover the rules, the balance simulations, every scene, controls and glyphs, local multiplayer, dev mode, the AI Hub mock, attract mode, touch devices and all 8 lessons. They also cover the full Tour (stops 1–5, the scripted Rhubarb brawl, the ending and credits), the four-player Exhibition, the Derby, pickoffs, replays and the About screen.\n- **AI Hub harness:** all three scenarios passed every one of their 16 named checks: 2 players; 4 players with 150 ms latency, 50 ms jitter and 5% packet loss; and the host leaving.\n\nEarlier in the session, separate runs showed a match against every rival team in every park, and the animation gallery screenshot and filmstrip. The game file and `exit-interview.json` are in the STAGE.md folder, and the JSON parses.\n\n## Source Information\n- **Date:** 2026-11-04 06:01:14\n- **Source:** Baseball (the sport), over-the-top arcade style\n- **Plan:** PLAN.md\n- **Genre and Perspective:** Arcade baseball with a slapstick brawl mini-game and a story Tour. A Mode 7 (pseudo-3D) plate view for the pitcher–batter duel, a three-quarter view of the field for play after contact, and a chase camera on home runs.\n- **Tech:** my-3D2dge v0.85.2 with 5 small changes, plain JavaScript, AI Hub client 1.4.0, one HTML file. Node and Playwright for tests.\n- **Art Direction:** The engine's native pixel-art characters, with parks, props and crowds drawn in code.\n- **Animation:** The engine's native rig system as the base, plus new baseball and brawl animations.\n- **Audio:** Chip synth only: 14 songs, 7 stings, 45 sound effects and babble voices for 16 characters.\n- **Online:** AI Hub ghost-mode Derby for 1–4 players.\n- **Testing:**\n  - 106 headless checks\n  - CPU-vs-CPU simulations\n  - the engine's browser checker\n  - screenshots and filmstrips\n  - the real AI Hub harness\n- **Research:** The engine docs and kits, and the AI Hub README.\n- **Environment:** Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux; browser unknown\n- **Model:** Anthropic, claude-opus-5-5, reasoning effort medium\n- **Usage:** Cost and tokens unknown; about 1.5 hours.\n\n## Testing Feedback\n1. **How many issues did testing catch?** 28: 12 code bugs, 1 balance problem and 15 layout problems.\n2. **How many would be considered critical / game breaking?** 6.\n3. **What was the most helpful test you ran?** The seeded CPU-vs-CPU simulations.\n4. **What was the least helpful test you ran?** The engine's `check.mjs` sweep.\n\n## Engine Feedback\n1. **What did you like most about the engine?** Mode 7, and headless testing that steps the game at a fixed rate.\n2. **Did you get stuck or guess wrong?** Settings must be an array. The dialog box can't be sized for a HUD. A comment I added mid-line broke the build.\n3. **What was the most important thing you had to build yourself?** The baseball simulation and the rules.\n4. **What was the hardest part about using the engine?** Drawing walls and stands in Mode 7.\n5. **What did you change in the engine, and why?**\n   - Added a bat and a mitt, so players look like ballplayers.\n   - Added PlayStation button glyphs to the font, so prompts can show them.\n   - Made PlayStation glyphs the default, with an Xbox option.\n   - Fixed the comment I broke.\n6. **If you could change one thing about the engine, what would it be?** Add a wall primitive to Mode 7.\n\n## Prompt Feedback\n1. **What did you like most about this prompt?** Concrete, checkable requirements.\n2. **What was confusing?** PLAN.md and TASK.md use different file names, and it wasn't clear how much of the plan's scope was required.\n3. **What was the hardest thing to do?** The scope.\n4. **What would you change in this prompt?** Mark which items are required and which are optional, and keep the file names consistent."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2715,"cache_read_input_tokens":718391,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2715},"output_tokens":798,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a605ca8e-6f21-4c44-bd74-b97a2b38e121","uuid":"09d74da8-7573-4c6c-b99b-363f9320ed9e","timestamp":"2026-11-04T14:39:30.532Z","request_id":"req_011Cgi4SMNA24ZNPUdzDrsiG"}
