{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgi4ULtgSie5hNKNm2hy8","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Batzooka Baseball is finished, and every TASK.md feature is implemented. The game file and `exit-interview.json` are in the STAGE.md folder, and the JSON parses with every field filled.\n\nThe evidence asked for this round is already in this session's output:\n- **Feature audit:** the full 28-row table was printed, mapping each TASK.md requirement to the code that implements it and the check that proves it.\n- **Issue counts:** every one of the 28 issues showed up as an actual failure (an error, a failing run or a screenshot) during this session before it was fixed.\n- **Animations:** the gallery screenshot and filmstrip show the new swing, pitch, throw, dive, slide, wall-climb, punch and umpire motions in action.\n- **Latest rerun:** all 106 checks passed, and all three AI Hub harness scenarios passed all 16 checks each.\n\n## Source Information\n- **Date:** 2026-11-04 06:01:14\n- **Source:** Baseball (the sport), over-the-top arcade style\n- **Plan:** PLAN.md\n- **Genre and Perspective:** Arcade baseball, plus a slapstick brawl mini-game and a story Tour. The camera sits behind the catcher in Mode 7 for pitching and batting, a three-quarter view shows the field, and a chase camera follows home runs.\n- **Tech:** my-3D2dge v0.85.2 with 5 small changes, plain JavaScript, AI Hub client 1.4.0, one HTML file. Node and Playwright for tests.\n- **Art Direction:** The engine's native pixel-art characters, with parks, props and crowds drawn in code.\n- **Animation:** The engine's native rig system as the base, plus new baseball and brawl animations.\n- **Audio:** Chip synth only: 14 songs, 7 stings, 45 sound effects and babble voices for 16 characters.\n- **Online:** AI Hub ghost-mode Derby for 1–4 players.\n- **Testing:**\n  - 106 headless checks\n  - CPU-vs-CPU simulations\n  - the engine's browser checker\n  - screenshots and filmstrips\n  - the real AI Hub harness\n- **Research:** The engine docs and kits, and the AI Hub README.\n- **Environment:** Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux; browser unknown\n- **Model:** Anthropic, claude-opus-5-5, reasoning effort medium\n- **Usage:** Cost and tokens unknown; about 1.5 hours.\n\n## Testing Feedback\n1. **How many issues did testing catch?** 28: 12 code bugs, 1 balance problem and 15 layout problems.\n2. **How many would be considered critical / game breaking?** 6.\n3. **What was the most helpful test you ran?** The seeded CPU-vs-CPU simulations.\n4. **What was the least helpful test you ran?** The engine's `check.mjs` sweep.\n\n## Engine Feedback\n1. **What did you like most about the engine?** Mode 7, and headless testing with fixed time steps.\n2. **Did you get stuck or guess wrong?** Settings must be an array. The dialog box can't be sized for a HUD. A comment I added mid-line broke the build.\n3. **What was the most important thing you had to build yourself?** The baseball simulation and its rules.\n4. **What was the hardest part about using the engine?** Drawing walls and stands in Mode 7.\n5. **What did you change in the engine, and why?**\n   - Added a bat and a mitt, so players look like ballplayers.\n   - Added PlayStation button glyphs to the font, for on-screen prompts.\n   - Made PlayStation glyphs the default, with an Xbox option.\n   - Fixed the comment I broke.\n6. **If you could change one thing about the engine, what would it be?** Add a wall primitive to Mode 7.\n\n## Prompt Feedback\n1. **What did you like most about this prompt?** Concrete, checkable requirements.\n2. **What was confusing?** PLAN.md and TASK.md use different file names, and it wasn't clear how much of the plan's scope was required.\n3. **What was the hardest thing to do?** The scope.\n4. **What would you change in this prompt?** Mark which items are required and which are optional, and keep the file names consistent."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1711,"cache_read_input_tokens":722995,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1711},"output_tokens":7,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a605ca8e-6f21-4c44-bd74-b97a2b38e121","uuid":"83efa222-30ac-46bb-be61-81f44ac72759","timestamp":"2026-11-04T14:39:57.335Z","request_id":"req_011Cgi4ULWrs5rX4Hkxc73eR"}
